FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-STRATEGIC-STOPLIST-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Controller adjudication — what I accept from the strategic review, what I do not, and what only the owner can settle
     2	Recorded 2026-09-10 against the two independent strategic reviews of 2026-09-09/10. Neither review is binding; both were commissioned by me and neither was given the owner's two hard requirements as a constraint. That omission matters for exactly one item below.
     3	
     4	## The six stops, ruled one by one
     5	
     6	**Stop the six-arm, many-seed success panel.** *Accept.* Six arms and many learner seeds ahead of one useful learned decision procedure is expensive rehearsal of an unanswered question. Nothing is being run on that path today.
     7	
     8	**Stop growing the corpus toward 51k–93k labels on the strength of an extrapolated curve.** *Accept, with the reason restated.* The decisive observation is not the extrapolation, it is that at the largest measured point the head still loses on both regret and realised efficiency — 10.3098 against 10.3178 Mbit/J — while its exact-best frequency improves. More accurate values have not yet produced a better rule. Growth resumes only if a measurement shows accuracy converting into decisions.
     9	
    10	**Stop treating a larger timeout or faster certification as the fix for the unilateral comparator.** *Accept.* The profiling shows genuinely late winners, 41 to 86 improving iterations and a longest uncensored run of 1,213 s. The tail is real work, not proof overhead. The two-arm split — offline certification for diagnosis, a separately declared anytime comparator for evaluation — is already required by contract v1.2 item 6, so this is not a new gate.
    11	
    12	**Stop sweeping the disputed circuit constant as a rescue.** *Accept.* The fixed-assignment sensitivity already answered whether that constant creates the sign; it does not, and the effect is larger at zero watts. More points do not address the real objection.
    13	
    14	**Stop broad defect adjudication as the default activity.** *Accept in principle, and I am the one who has been violating it.* Repair only what the selected result needs.
    15	
    16	**Stop rebuilding the first two heads merely to preserve the three-component story.** *Reject, on the owner's standing requirement.* The review is right that the mechanism study does not need them, and right that repairing two surrogates to protect a narrative is bad science. But the owner's requirement is not narrative: each of the three components must genuinely raise pooled efficiency, and publishing a negative for one of them is explicitly not acceptable. The sufficiency diagnostic has since shown that on the current encoders the first head has held-out explained variance of −0.336 — worse than predicting the mean — with a proved collision that no deterministic predictor can escape. Under that defect a three-head run cannot be a fair test of the first two, and a null from it would be uninterpretable. So the encoder repair is a **precondition for answering the owner's question at all**, not a rescue of a story. It stays. The review did not have this requirement in front of it.
    17	
    18	## Where the review anticipated today's result
    19	Its closing section asked whether the occupancy blackout should exist at all, and proposed comparing a service-aware power policy that can allocate enough power for a feasible mode without waiting for two more users to arrive. The ladder job, dispatched before I read that section, is running precisely that comparison, and its interim numbers already show zero no-mode events under margin provisioning against 55.7 % under the sealed law. The review called this "a new scientific intervention, not a permissible silent change to the sealed benchmark", and it is being run that way: on a copy, with the declared physics untouched.
    20	
    21	If the coordination gain largely survives the change, the mechanism claim strengthens and gains a much better story — a genuine convexity between superlinear power growth under consolidation and per-chain circuit cost under spreading. If it largely vanishes, the contribution becomes a diagnosis of the control law and its remedy, which the review judges potentially more useful than teaching three networks to compensate for it. Either way the ladder job decides it, and I will not pre-empt it.
    22	
    23	## Three cautions I am adopting as constraints on how anything gets written
    24	- The bounded-search advantage is **not** a mathematical ceiling. Its comparator is one specified unilateral procedure's local fixed point, not the best obtainable by every unilateral strategy and not a certified global optimum. The claim is that coordinated moves improve those certified local endpoints.
    25	- "Served" in the current instrumentation means positive decoding time. It is **not** rate-target attainment and **not** uninterrupted service, so the 1,939→1,957 improvement does not by itself discharge the contracted service conditions.
    26	- No number of anchors or seeds converts one completed ephemeris date into independent date replication.
    27	
    28	## Owner decisions this does not settle
    29	The reviews split on the evaluation date pool and one of them proposed three further options; the comparator positioning, the beamwidth convention and the strategic reframing itself all remain the owner's. Recorded here only so that accepting five of six stops is not mistaken for accepting the reframing.
FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-CEILING-INTERVAL-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Controller finding — the headroom now has an interval, and it is stable across dates
     2	Recorded 2026-09-10 from the thirty-date coordination-headroom diagnostic. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. No learner; no sealed value changed.
     3	
     4	## The number the strategic review asked for
     5	Both strategic reviews named the same weakest point: the coordination headroom was a single figure with no interval. It now has one.
     6	
     7	Across **30 TRAIN dates**, treating the date as the independent unit — each date pools bits and joules across its anchors, computes each arm's pooled efficiency, then forms the ratio — the mean gain of the bounded joint selector over the certified unilateral fixed point is **+5.888 %**, date-level sample SD **1.747 %**, two-sided 95 % interval **[+5.235 %, +6.540 %]**.
     8	
     9	**All thirty dates are positive.** Minimum +3.205 % on 2026-07-17, maximum +9.652 % on 2025-09-30. The twenty dates spanning the full archive give +5.978 % and a single-month panel of ten January dates gives +5.706 %, so the effect is not an artefact of the date spread.
    10	
    11	Pooling all 196 anchors regardless of date gives +5.926 %, reported as a separate weighting and deliberately not used for the interval, because it weights dates by their energies and by unequal anchor counts.
    12	
    13	## Two facts that close off easy objections
    14	The panel runs from 2025-07-31 to 2026-08-20, over which the constellation grows from **8,044 to 10,746 satellites**. The correlation between a date's gain and its satellite count is **−0.122** over all thirty dates and −0.166 within the full-span twenty. So the variation across dates is **not constellation growth**; it is time-varying geometry. Every selected daily ephemeris file has zero quarantined records.
    15	
    16	## What it does and does not establish
    17	It establishes that the effect the project measured on a narrow panel is **stable across dates** under the physics as it was then implemented. It is a descriptive interval over the selected dates, not a population-randomisation interval.
    18	
    19	**Every one of these numbers was computed under the provisioning rule since shown defective** — the one that credits nothing on about three quarters of transmission instances and attains the per-user rate target for none of 2,000 users. So the interval is an interval on an artefact.
    20	
    21	## Why it still matters, and what was dispatched
    22	Two things survive the defect. The **method** — thirty dates, the date as the independent unit, per-date receipts, a refuse-to-overwrite guard — is exactly what the corrected measurement needs. And the **spread** is the warning: this quantity varies by a factor of three across dates, with a date-level SD of 1.747 %.
    23	
    24	That matters because every judgement made today about whether the project has a future rests on a single corrected-physics figure of about +0.51 %, measured on **one** twenty-anchor panel drawn from four worlds. If the corrected quantity has comparable relative variation, its true value could be materially smaller or larger than that one measurement, and those two cases imply different decisions.
    25	
    26	The same thirty-date panel under the corrected rule is therefore running, with a bit-identity assertion required on at least three dates before any of its output is admissible.
    27	
    28	## Cost, for planning
    29	About eight minutes of wall clock and 0.3 core-hours per date at eight to ten anchors; roughly ten core-hours for the panel.
FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-CORRECTED-PICTURE-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Controller finding — the corrected-physics coordination picture, from two panels
     2	Recorded 2026-09-10 from the strict-clearance beam-width curve and the thirty-date corrected panel. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. No learner, no training run, no policy run; nothing sealed modified.
     3	
     4	## The numerical-implementation question is settled
     5	Two implementations of the corrected provisioning existed, and an adjudication blocked a decision until the stricter one had produced a full five-width curve. It has:
     6	
     7	| one-sided width | simple division | **strict clearance** | difference |
     8	|---:|---:|---:|---:|
     9	| **1.66°** (sealed) | −0.3028 % (5/8 negative) | **−0.1768 % (3/8 negative)** | +0.126 |
    10	| 2.40° | +1.2089 % | **+1.9483 %** | +0.739 |
    11	| **3.32°** (the source's own value) | +0.9848 % | **+2.3460 %** | **+1.361** |
    12	| 4.50° | +3.2052 % | +3.0077 % | −0.197 |
    13	| 6.65° | +7.3153 % | **+8.1628 %** | +0.847 |
    14	
    15	**No sign changes.** Both remain negative only at the sealed width, so the attempt to rescue a positive value through the stricter numerics fails — exactly as the adjudication predicted.
    16	
    17	**The shape does change**, and this corrects something I reported to the owner. Simple division dips from +1.209 % at 2.40° to +0.985 % at 3.32°; strict clearance rises at **every** sampled step. My statement that the monotone rise "does not survive" was an artefact of the defective numerics: under the correct implementation it does survive.
    18	
    19	## Thirty dates under the corrected rule
    20	**Mean +0.717 %, sample SD 0.751 %, 95 % interval [+0.436 %, +0.997 %], positive on 26 of 30 dates.** The four negatives are small: −0.075 %, −0.070 %, −0.265 % and −0.230 %. Maximum +3.246 %.
    21	
    22	The report leads with the honest reading and I adopt it: **the corrected gap is small and its interval includes practically immaterial values.**
    23	
    24	Its compatibility gate is the standard I want everywhere: before any corrected date was run, the copied evaluator was compiled with its divisor set to one and three complete six-anchor dates rerun, with **every deterministic receipt field bit-identical** — world identity, seed, epoch, search paths and counts, terminal certificates, configuration identifiers, committed bits, joules and served counts, and summaries — excluding only wall and CPU timing.
    25	
    26	## The finding I did not anticipate
    27	The Spearman rank correlation between the per-date gains under the two provisioning rules is **ρ = +0.006**. Which dates favour coordination under the sealed rule tells you **nothing** about which favour it under the corrected one, and four dates flip from favourable to non-positive. Any date-selection intuition carried over from the sealed rule is worthless.
    28	
    29	## Both panels carry the old pairing
    30	| panel | pairing | corrected span |
    31	|---|---|---:|
    32	| twenty anchors | **correct** | **+1.29 %** |
    33	| thirty dates | old | +0.717 % [+0.436, +0.997] |
    34	| five widths | old | −0.177 % at the sealed width |
    35	
    36	Both of the latter were started before the pairing defect was found. On the twenty-anchor panel correct pairing raised the corrected figure by 0.75 points. **I am not extrapolating that**; the five-width curve is being re-measured with strict clearance and correct pairing together, and the thirty-date panel's transferable value is its variance structure rather than its point estimate.
    37	
    38	## Where this leaves the coordination side
    39	Small, positive, with an interval whose lower edge approaches immateriality. Three routes must each show a resolvable positive marginal inside that band. It is tight — but the owner's bar is an ordering rather than a fixed per-contrast threshold, and a leave-one-out arm can fall **below** the fixed point, so the marginals are not bounded by the band.
FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-SEARCH-ORDER-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Controller finding — every coordination number today is paired against the wrong baseline
     2	Recorded 2026-09-10, derived by placing two of today's reports side by side rather than by any new run. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. Nothing sealed changed; a corrected measurement is running.
     3	
     4	## What the arithmetic says
     5	The anytime measurement reports that accepting the **first** strict improvement, rather than completing a best-improvement sweep, changes the search path and the fixed point on **all twenty anchors under both provisioning rules**, and converges **8.13 % above** the archived endpoint under the sealed rule and **1.62 % above** it under the corrected one.
     6	
     7	Applying those to the archived pooled figures:
     8	
     9	| sealed rule | pooled efficiency, Mbit/J |
    10	|---|---:|
    11	| archived unilateral, best-improvement | 28.4709 |
    12	| **archived bounded joint selector** | **30.2814** |
    13	| **first-improvement unilateral** | **≈ 30.79** |
    14	
    15	The sixty-second row of the anytime curve gives the same answer independently: 29.5396 is 95.39 % of the first-improvement prize, which puts convergence at about 30.787.
    16	
    17	Under the corrected rule the first-improvement endpoint lands near 43.71 against the archived joint selector's 43.24.
    18	
    19	**Under both rules, changing nothing but the order in which the local search accepts improvements produces a unilateral endpoint that exceeds the bounded joint selector it was supposed to be beaten by.**
    20	
    21	## What this does and does not license
    22	It does **not** license "coordination is worthless". The joint selector was **seeded from the best-improvement fixed point**. Re-seeding it from the better endpoint should improve it too, and it may still win.
    23	
    24	What it licenses is narrower and worse: **the comparison as run is mispaired.** Every coordination figure the project holds — the archived +6.359 %, the corrected +0.51 %, the five-point beam-width curve, the thirty-date interval and its confidence bounds — measures a joint selector seeded from one local optimum against that same local optimum, when a different traversal order of the same neighbourhood reaches a better one. **The real span is unknown.**
    25	
    26	This is also the concrete form of a caution the provisioning adjudication gave and I did not fully absorb: the unilateral certificate establishes local optimality **in the specified neighbourhood**, and the joint result establishes a maximum **over its bounded candidate family**. Neither is a global optimum, and neither is invariant to the traversal order. We have been treating one particular local optimum as though the word "certified" made it canonical.
    27	
    28	## What is running
    29	A four-arm re-measurement on the same twenty anchors under both rules: the two unilateral endpoints, the joint selector seeded from each, and both cross pairings so that the seed effect and the search-order effect can be separated. Its first line must state the correctly paired span, and it is instructed to lead with the fact if that span is near zero or negative.
    30	
    31	## Standing
    32	No result is withdrawn yet, because the corrected pairing has not been measured. But no coordination figure recorded today should be carried forward until it has been.
FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-SPAN-AND-C3-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Controller finding — the corrected span is more than double what I reported, and the third route is not a size penalty
     2	Recorded 2026-09-10 from two pre-declared measurements that landed within a minute of each other. Both reuse frozen splits, seeds, estimator families and tie-breaks from earlier work; neither tuned any scorer. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. No learner deployed, no training run, no policy run, nothing sealed modified.
     3	
     4	## The coordination span, correctly paired
     5	Every span recorded today compared a joint selector seeded from one local optimum against that same optimum, when a different traversal order of the same neighbourhood reaches a better one. Re-measured with **both arms on the better search**:
     6	
     7	| rule | mispaired | **correctly paired** | negative anchors |
     8	|---|---:|---:|---:|
     9	| sealed | +6.3590 % | **+4.6046 %** | 1 of 20 |
    10	| **corrected** | **+0.5448 %** | **+1.2913 %** | 6 of 20 |
    11	
    12	**Under the corrected physics the span is more than double what I have been reporting all day.** The mispairing overstated the sealed figure by 1.75 points and **understated** the corrected one by 0.75 points — opposite directions, which is why no ratio may be used to extrapolate the other figures.
    13	
    14	My inference that the better unilateral endpoint would overtake the archived joint selector was correct — 30.7869 against 30.2814 under the sealed rule. But the joint selector re-seeded from that better endpoint overtakes it again, at **32.2045**. **Coordination is real, not an artefact of traversal order.**
    15	
    16	The two sign counts answer different questions and must not be merged: on the selection-time objective the joint selector strictly improves on its seed at **20 of 20** anchors under both rules; on the forty-eight-boundary committed efficiency it is positive at 19 of 20 under the sealed rule and 14 of 20 under the corrected one.
    17	
    18	One detail worth keeping: under the corrected rule the better unilateral endpoint delivers **fewer** bits than the archived one, 3.169 against 3.202 Tbit, while spending far less energy, 72,516 against 74,453 J. First-improvement trades bits for energy there.
    19	
    20	## The third route is not a size penalty
    21	A design reviewer's specific objection was that the interaction route's correction is a large, nearly size-proportional term, and that until the system beats a fixed per-size prior the honest description is that the sum needs a size penalty and this route supplies one. Tested:
    22	
    23	| scorer | held-out mean selection regret |
    24	|---|---:|
    25	| **learned interaction head** | **3.618** |
    26	| size-only prior | 13.114 |
    27	| zero interaction | 13.683 |
    28	
    29	The learned head's advantage over the size prior is **9.496**; the size prior's advantage over zero is **0.569**. **Knowing the coalition size is worth almost nothing; nearly all of the learned head's value is set-specific.**
    30	
    31	The fitted prior is instructive rather than weak: it does capture the large negative at size one hundred, at −12.402 against small positives at sizes two to four, and it still lands at 13.114. Reproducing the size effect is not the same as ranking.
    32	
    33	## What this changes and what it does not
    34	It raises my estimate for the third route materially — its one named threat is now tested and failed — and it more than doubles the budget the three routes have to share under corrected physics.
    35	
    36	It does **not** measure the owner's requirement. Both results are offline measurements on labelled candidate pools with exact labels, not closed-loop policy runs, and the source-training contrast over the three routes has still never been run at scale.
    37	
    38	## An immediate consequence for a result I reported tonight
    39	The five-point beam-width curve was computed with the same mispairing. I told the owner that coordination is **negative** at the width we currently model, at −0.303 %. On the twenty-anchor panel that same mispairing understated the corrected span by a factor of 2.4. That curve must be recomputed with correct pairing before the "this design point is dead" conclusion stands. I am not extrapolating the factor; it must be measured.
FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-CONTRADICTION-RESIDUAL-SIGN-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Open contradiction — the residual's sign flips between two measurements
     2	
     3	**2026-09-10. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. Recorded while unresolved, deliberately. No sealed
     4	artefact, constant, threshold, sign, seed, horizon, price, guard or acceptance rule is
     5	changed. This record exists so the contradiction cannot later be quietly resolved in whichever
     6	direction turns out to be convenient.**
     7	
     8	**Two receipts, both complete, disagree on the sign of the exact set residual's effect on
     9	pooled reported EE. `RESIDTOGGLE` reports `+5.62%`. `C3REACH` reports `-60%`. Neither is
    10	being preferred here.**
    11	
    12	## The two receipts
    13	
    14	| | `RESIDTOGGLE` | `C3REACH` |
    15	|---|---|---|
    16	| report | `ORACLE-RESIDUAL-TOGGLE-2026-09-10.md` | `C3-ARGMAX-REACHABILITY-2026-09-10.md` |
    17	| worlds | `V025_PROBE_R2/world/1`, `/2` | `V025_PROBE/world/3` |
    18	| anchors | 8 | 20 (x 4 lineages = 80 decisions) |
    19	| catalogue | purpose-built, 8,192 cap, singletons + bundles + evacuations + rung controls | pilot's deployed `_build_anchor_rows(full_legal_actions=True)` + `_catalogue_with_census`, 948-1000 rows |
    20	| **price / objective** | **exact-Fraction Dinkelbach, one common price across all eight anchors, per numerator** | **the pilot's own score: additive + interaction, boundary-0 `F = B - eta_ref*E` in kappa units** |
    21	| exact residual effect, demand-capped | **+5.62%** (`8.548697 -> 9.029226` Mbit/J) | **30.82 -> 12.30 Mbit/J** over the 48 changed decisions |
    22	| mechanism visible in the receipt | served `486 -> 503`, target attained `181 -> 192` | capped bits `6.219e12 -> 4.825e12`, **energy `201,800 -> 392,255 J`** |
    23	
    24	## What both agree on
    25	
    26	- **The residual is reachable.** `RESIDTOGGLE`: the two selectors differ at **8/8** anchors.
    27	  `C3REACH`: exact `Psi` changes the argmax at **14/20** anchors, learned `Psi` at **20/20**.
    28	  The earlier "C3 is structurally inert" reading is dead by two independent routes, and
    29	  erratum 15 and erratum 16 are confirmed rather than merely argued.
    30	- **Tie-breaks are not doing the work.** `C3REACH`: 0/80 final-ranking tie-break flips, and
    31	  the top two rows were within 1 ULP in 0/80 rankings under every scoring variant.
    32	- **The learned head is badly scaled.** Learned `Psi` spans 2,518-11,205 against an additive
    33	  score spread of 107-264 at the same anchor - one to two orders of magnitude. It dominates
    34	  the ranking rather than adjusting it. This independently confirms a worker's report that
    35	  the learned head is "off by two orders of magnitude at the grand row" and reaches the
    36	  decision "destructively".
    37	- **`contexts.get(...)` is `None` on 79.164%** of pooled legal rows, so the residual can only
    38	  reorder about a fifth of any catalogue. It still flips 70% of anchors within that fifth.
    39	
    40	## Candidate explanations, none established
    41	
    42	1. **Objective mismatch.** `RESIDTOGGLE` selects under a price solved to target pooled EE;
    43	   `C3REACH` selects under the pilot's boundary-0 `F`. If the pilot's selection objective is
    44	   misaligned with the reported numerator, a large-magnitude term would **amplify** that
    45	   misalignment - which is consistent with energy nearly doubling in `C3REACH`. **`OBJMISMATCH`
    46	   is measuring exactly this and has not reported.**
    47	2. **Different worlds.** `world/3` versus `world/1` and `/2`.
    48	3. **Different catalogues.** A purpose-built catalogue with evacuations and bundles versus the
    49	   pilot's deployed catalogue.
    50	4. **Different residual object.** `RESIDTOGGLE` adds `joint - sum(singletons)` reconstructing
    51	   the candidate surplus exactly; `C3REACH` adds `_exact_interactions` under the production
    52	   `contexts` gate, which is absent on 79% of rows. **These may not be the same quantity.**
    53	
    54	Explanation 1 would mean the fault is in the **scoring objective**, not in the route - and
    55	would be repairable without touching any of the three routes. Explanation 4 would mean the two
    56	jobs measured **different things** and neither is wrong. I have evidence for neither.
    57	
    58	## The rule I am binding myself to
    59	
    60	- **Neither receipt is preferred, cited alone, or quietly dropped.** Any later statement about
    61	  the residual's value must carry both numbers until the contradiction is resolved by
    62	  measurement.
    63	- The resolution must come from a measurement that **discriminates** between the candidates
    64	  above - at minimum, running both scoring treatments on the **same** world, anchors and
    65	  catalogue. That measurement is to be declared before it runs.
    66	- **`RESIDTOGGLE`'s `+5.62%` remains reported against the pre-declared 10% and 5% screens**
    67	  exactly as it was, and the pre-declared reading rule for it is unchanged. This record does
    68	  not retract it; it records that a second measurement disagrees.
    69	- If the contradiction resolves in the direction that makes the work harder, it is reported
    70	  the same way and in the same detail as if it had gone the other way.
FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Pre-declaration — the §C3 screening run, fixed before the harness finished and before any contrast existed
     2	Recorded 2026-09-10. The protocol below was written into the dispatch prompt before the run and is recorded here so it survives independently of the server. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`, and additionally **`SCREEN_NOT_CONFIRMATORY`**: no result from this run may be reported as the answer to the owner's requirement.
     3	
     4	## What is being run, and why it matters
     5	Contract §C3 — the source-training contrast — **for the first time**. For each of three learned routes, that route's training source is replaced by a neutral one while **all heads are retained, updated and deployed**. Neutral never means removing a head.
     6	
     7	## The arms: the complete factorial, plus one external reference
     8	Eight learned arms, being all eight cells of {informative, neutral} over three routes:
     9	
    10	| arm | first | second | third |
    11	|---|:-:|:-:|:-:|
    12	| full | I | I | I |
    13	| leave-one-out ×3 | N/I/I | I/N/I | I/I/N |
    14	| single-informative ×3 | I/N/N | N/I/N | N/N/I |
    15	| all-neutral control | N | N | N |
    16	
    17	Plus the external geometry-only baseline, which has no learner at all. The sealed panel contains five of these eight cells; the three single-informative arms are the addition the owner's requirement needs, and without them the leave-one-in half of that requirement cannot be evaluated at all.
    18	
    19	## Fixed before the run
    20	- **Both provisioning rules.** A result under the sealed rule alone would be measured on a model crediting nothing on three quarters of its transmissions; under the corrected rule alone it would prejudge a decision the owner has not taken.
    21	- **Sealed learning rates and architectures, untouched**: first route 1.0e-2 with one hidden layer of eight and ReLU; second 1.0e-3 with 100-50-50 and tanh; third 1.0e-3 with 64-64 and ReLU; Adam at the sealed betas and epsilon; one deterministic full-batch update per route per source epoch. **If a route fails to train, that is the finding.**
    22	- **Two learner seeds**, reported seedwise, supporting no distributional claim.
    23	- **Nine thousand source epochs. Checkpoints every 100. Full panel evaluation at exactly 500, 1000, 2000, 4000 and 9000. The contrast is reported at 9000**; the four earlier evaluations are trajectory and none may be reported as the outcome.
    24	
    25	The separation matters: training an epoch and saving a checkpoint are nearly free, while evaluating the panel across arms, anchors and forty-eight boundaries is the expensive operation. **The budget therefore controls evaluation count, not epoch count** — which is why the horizon is nine thousand rather than the two thousand I first proposed. The owner made that point and it was correct.
    26	
    27	- **A cost-driven early stop is legitimate** at whichever declared evaluation point was reached, with the measured figures that forced it. A stop chosen because a point looked favourable is not, and the distinction must be visible.
    28	
    29	## Convergence rule, declared now
    30	- validation objective still falling at the end → **under-trained**; the remedy is more epochs, **not** a different learning rate;
    31	- oscillating without settling → **that route's rate is too high**;
    32	- flat early and high → rate too low, or capacity or features are the limit, needing diagnosis rather than a rate change.
    33	
    34	This exists so that the learning rates are not adjusted on the basis of the contrast they produce.
    35	
    36	## Why a declared reporting point at all
    37	A previous pilot moved from −2.4 % at 200 epochs, through −1.6 % at 1000, to +15.6 % at 2000. Choosing among those after the fact would bias everything downstream. Looking early is fine and is the point of the trajectory; **choosing afterwards is not**.
    38	
    39	## The primary deliverable is not the contrast
    40	It is the **training curves per route per arm**. Whether the routes converge, oscillate or are still climbing determines whether anything about the budget or the rates needs attention before a confirmatory run. A contrast from a route that never converged is not informative about that route.
    41	
    42	## Reading rule
    43	The degeneracy screen pre-declared earlier applies unchanged: below-reference by exact sign against the head-independent certified fixed point, with every contrast reported both over all anchors and over the subset where every arm in that contrast is at or above reference.
    44	
    45	## Audit
    46	Two independent pre-run audits of the harness were dispatched in parallel with the screen rather than before it, so that the audits read the code while the screen exercises it. If either reports a blocking defect the screen is stopped and re-run. The machine was idle, so the expected cost of parallelism is lower than the cost of serialising a thirty-minute audit in front of a multi-hour run.
FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-DECOMPOSITION-BAKEOFF-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Pre-declaration — head-to-head screen of the two candidate decompositions
     2	
     3	**2026-09-10, written BEFORE any exact-path row exists.** `EXACTGEN` is generating the
     4	corpus and has produced nothing yet. No sealed artefact, constant, threshold, sign, seed,
     5	horizon, price, guard or acceptance rule is changed. This fixes the comparison metrics while
     6	no data exists to tune them against.
     7	
     8	## The two candidates
     9	
    10	| | Partitions | Three routes | Cost to the claim |
    11	|---|---|---|---|
    12	| **F** (fable) | the **physical quantity** | credited bits under the candidate's occupancy; resource energy under the candidate's activation; continuation | **forfeits coordination as a named ablatable route** |
    13	| **A** (astra) | the **information** | local-link innovation; temporal innovation; relational innovation — successive increments of `E[Y \| I0, X_J]` where `Y = B - eta_ref*E` | keeps three named routes; **ablation must propagate through the whole computation**, not zero an output |
    14	
    15	They partition different axes, so they are not variants of one another and **neither is a
    16	special case of the other**.
    17	
    18	## What can and cannot run in parallel
    19	
    20	**Can, and should:**
    21	- Both derive every target from the same coupled-physics quantities — whole-network bits and
    22	  joules, per-user attribution, the three sealed offsets. `EXACTGEN` produces those once and
    23	  both consume them. **The expensive part is shared.**
    24	- Both can be screened **offline, with no training and no policy run**, by computing their
    25	  targets on the same rows and measuring the quantities below.
    26	- The mode-selection change (`R2`/`R3` stale-CQI) sits in the control law, not the route
    27	  layer, and is orthogonal to both.
    28	
    29	**Cannot:**
    30	- A contract v2 declaration names **one** set of three route identities. The choice is
    31	  exclusive **at declaration time**, not at measurement time.
    32	- Full training of both to endpoint would double the panel cost. This screen deliberately
    33	  stops before that.
    34	
    35	## Metrics, fixed now
    36	
    37	Computed for **F**, for **A**, and for the **incumbent** `Psi = Delta F(A) - sum d_i`, on the
    38	same rows, same anchors, same catalogue:
    39	
    40	1. **Pointwise conditioning.** Parts-to-total ratio `(sum |parts|) / |total|` at each
    41	   coalition size, and its growth in size. The incumbent's measured values are 1.57x at pairs
    42	   and 22.99x at the grand row; report every candidate on that same scale. Report the
    43	   **pointwise** figure for all three. A population RMS bound may be reported **alongside**
    44	   but never in place of it, and never compared directly against a pointwise number.
    45	2. **Reachability.** Fraction of anchors at which the third route's term changes the catalogue
    46	   argmax, computed **exactly** (with the exact term, not a learned head), plus the share of
    47	   catalogue rows the term can never reorder.
    48	3. **Learnability of each route, separately.** Held-out `R^2`, within-group pairwise ordering,
    49	   and top-1 argmax agreement, under leave-one-anchor-out and leave-one-world-out, against a
    50	   linear model, a constant predictor, and a high-capacity model on the same inputs. A
    51	   high-capacity failure means the ceiling is **informational**, not architectural.
    52	4. **Distinctness.** Pairwise correlation between the three routes' targets, and the `R^2` of
    53	   each route regressed on the other two. A route that is a function of the others is not a
    54	   separate source, whatever it is named.
    55	5. **Cost.** Wall time to produce each route's target per anchor, so the panel can be costed
    56	   before it is funded.
    57	
    58	## Reading rule, fixed now
    59	
    60	- **No winner is declared on conditioning alone.** Conditioning is necessary, not sufficient:
    61	  a perfectly conditioned decomposition whose routes are not separately learnable, or not
    62	  distinct, fails.
    63	- **A candidate that fails (2) — its third route cannot change the argmax — is rejected for
    64	  the three-route claim**, regardless of how well it scores elsewhere. It may still be
    65	  reported as a better total-score predictor.
    66	- **If both pass every metric**, the choice is **the owner's**, because the deciding question
    67	  is what the paper claims — whether "coordination" survives as a named ablatable route — and
    68	  that is not a measurement.
    69	- **If both fail**, that is reported plainly, with the incumbent's numbers beside them, and
    70	  no third candidate is invented to rescue the outcome in the same breath.
    71	- Nothing here is an EE claim. None of these metrics is pooled EE, and none may be reported
    72	  as one. Committed pooled EE is measured only on a declared panel, later, if one is funded.
    73	
    74	## What this pre-declaration is not
    75	
    76	It does not authorise contract v2, a corpus substitution, a panel, or any training. It fixes
    77	how two proposals will be compared, before either has a number attached.
FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-DEGENERACY-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Pre-declaration — the degeneracy screen for the §C3 panel, fixed before any §C3 number exists
     2	Recorded 2026-09-10, **before** the panel is built and before any source-training contrast has been measured. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. Nothing here changes an arm definition, a source, a catalogue rule, a price, a guard or an acceptance criterion; it fixes how the resulting numbers may be read.
     3	
     4	## The problem this prevents
     5	A leave-one-out arm ranks candidates with predicted scores, and its catalogue retains a fallback. A poorly informed head can therefore select something **worse** than the fallback. If it does, the gap between the full arm and that arm is large — and that largeness is evidence of the reference arm collapsing, not of the missing route contributing.
     6	
     7	One reviewer put the arithmetic plainly: a ranker can add at most the coordination span above the certified fixed point, so **any gap materially larger than that span means one arm fell below it**. On today's measurements that span is roughly one per cent, while a pilot produced a full-minus-drop gap of +15.6 %. I reported that gap to the owner as encouraging. It was not.
     8	
     9	## The reference, and why it is well defined
    10	The certified unilateral fixed point is produced by an exact best-response search over single-user deviations. **It consumes no head output**, so at a given anchor and provisioning rule there is exactly one such endpoint, shared by every arm. It is therefore a legitimate common reference and needs no per-arm construction.
    11	
    12	Which local search produces it must be stated: today's anytime work showed that accepting the first strict improvement reaches a **different and better** endpoint than completing a best-improvement sweep, on all twenty anchors under both rules. **The screen uses whichever search the panel's own arms are built on, and the panel must use one search for every arm.**
    13	
    14	## The screen, declared
    15	For every arm and every anchor, compute the committed forty-eight-boundary pooled efficiency of the arm's chosen configuration and of the certified unilateral fixed point at that same anchor.
    16	
    17	An arm is **below reference** at an anchor when its committed efficiency is strictly less than the fixed point's. No tolerance is applied: the comparison is by exact sign, so no threshold is chosen and none can later be argued about.
    18	
    19	Then report, for every contrast, **both** of the following:
    20	
    21	1. the marginal over **all** anchors;
    22	2. the marginal over the subset where **every arm in the contrast** is at or above reference.
    23	
    24	**If the two agree, nothing is at issue. If they diverge, the divergence is the finding**, and the all-anchor figure may not be presented as component evidence without the restricted figure beside it.
    25	
    26	Also report, per arm, the count and fraction of anchors below reference, and the distribution of the shortfall. An arm that is frequently below reference has a defect of its own, whatever its ordering says.
    27	
    28	## Why it is written this way
    29	No threshold is picked, so none can be tuned. The restricted subset is a standard sensitivity analysis rather than a filter chosen to produce an outcome. And both figures are published, so a reader can see exactly what the screen did.
    30	
    31	## What it does not do
    32	It does not decide whether a route contributes. It prevents one specific misreading. A route whose arm stays above reference and still shows a positive marginal is supported by this panel; a route whose apparent margin comes from its reference arm collapsing is not.
    33	
    34	## Standing
    35	Fixed on 2026-09-10, before the panel exists. If it is ever changed, the change and its reason must be recorded with a date, and any result produced under the earlier version must be reported under both.
FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-GEOMETRY-TEST-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Pre-declaration — the geometry-feature test for the first route, with my expectation stated before it runs
     2	Recorded 2026-09-10, **before dispatching** and before any result exists. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. Nothing here authorises a change to the sealed feature schema; it declares a diagnostic and the prediction it will be judged against.
     3	
     4	## What will be tested
     5	Two candidate features for the per-user route, both **action-local** and both computable from the decision-time tape without any coupled solve:
     6	
     7	- the **off-axis angle** of the focal user under the candidate beam, replacing the hard-coded zero that both row-building paths currently write;
     8	- the **elevation angle** of the candidate beam's satellite at the focal user, for which no feature slot exists at all.
     9	
    10	The arms, metrics, split, seed, estimator family and grid will be those of the two comparisons already run today, so the result is directly comparable to the resource-context test that failed. The primary metric is **held-out pairwise ordering within each anchor's candidate pool**, the same quantity measured at 0.650 for this route and 0.902 for an oracle that removes only the cross-user externality. The materiality rule already frozen for that test applies unchanged.
    11	
    12	## My expectation, stated now
    13	**I expect the gain to be small, and I would not be surprised by zero.**
    14	
    15	The reason against: if the nominal margin at the rate target is exact, it already contains the antenna gain and the path — for the **focal link** the angle is a sufficient statistic and adds nothing beyond it.
    16	
    17	The reason for: the target is a whole-network difference, and 79.3 % of its variance is externality — how *other* users' links change. That depends on angular geometry between beams, which the focal link's margin does not express. The raw angle at least locates the focal user in the pattern, and so hints how much of the focal beam's power spills into neighbours.
    18	
    19	The hole in that reason: what actually determines the spill is the **neighbours'** geometry, not the focal angle alone. That is precisely what the 163 resource-context coordinates encode, and they failed today — rebuilt per focal action, only 28 of them varied at all.
    20	
    21	So the mechanism that would make this work is the same one that has already been measured not to work, approached from a thinner direction.
    22	
    23	## Why it is still worth one measurement
    24	It is cheap, the harness exists, and the candidate is **not** in the class that failed for a structural reason: the resource-context coordinates failed because their useful variation is coalition-level while this route's interface is action-local. An angle is action-local. So this test distinguishes "the interface cannot carry the information" from "this particular information does not help", which are different diagnoses with different consequences.
    25	
    26	And the hard-coded zero is a defect regardless of what the test shows: a slot the designers provided, filled with a constant, at both row-building sites.
    27	
    28	## The standard this is held to
    29	If the gain is immaterial, the record will show I predicted it, and the first route will have had three repairs measured and rejected — at which point the honest next step is to stop proposing repairs and run the contrast, letting the route answer for itself.
    30	
    31	If the gain is material, the surprise is itself information: it would mean the externality is partly predictable from focal geometry, which nothing measured so far suggests.
    32	
    33	Either way the prediction is on the record before the measurement, which is the point.
FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-RESIDUAL-READING-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Pre-declaration — how the residual-ceiling result will be read
     2	
     3	**2026-09-10, written BEFORE either measurement has reported.** No sealed artefact,
     4	constant, threshold, sign, seed, horizon, price, guard or acceptance rule is changed by this
     5	record. Its only purpose is to fix the reading rule while the outcome is still unknown.
     6	
     7	## What is being measured
     8	
     9	- **RESIDTOGGLE** — over one fixed catalogue at 8 anchors under corrected physics,
    10	  `ADDITIVE_ONLY` versus `WITH_RESIDUAL` in the **deployed selector**, scored on the
    11	  **reported** objective: pooled committed EE over 48 boundaries, demand-capped. This is the
    12	  ceiling on what **any** C3 head can be worth inside the deployed selector, because it gives
    13	  the residual exactly rather than predicting it.
    14	- **OBJMISMATCH** — whether the certified endpoints are locally optimal under the **reported**
    15	  objective, as opposed to the boundary-0 selection objective `F = B - eta_ref E` they were
    16	  certified against.
    17	
    18	## The screens, as the two strategic reviews stated them
    19	
    20	| Reviewer | Screen |
    21	|---|---|
    22	| astra | **10%** |
    23	| fable | **5%**, and required on **both** halves |
    24	
    25	Both were stated before either measurement ran. **They are not adjusted here and will not be
    26	adjusted after the fact.**
    27	
    28	## The reading rule
    29	
    30	Let `R` be the residual ceiling RESIDTOGGLE reports on the reported numerator.
    31	
    32	- **`R` at or above 10%** — both screens pass. The current decomposition can in principle
    33	  support a substantial C3 contribution, and repairing the panel harness is justified. The
    34	  repair order is the owed-repair register in
    35	  `V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-CORPUS-IS-SURROGATE-2026-09-10.md` section 5, not a new plan.
    36	- **`R` between 5% and 10%** — the reviewers' screens disagree on this interval. **This is
    37	  not mine to resolve by preference.** It goes to the owner with both screens stated, both
    38	  numbers stated, and no unilateral call.
    39	- **`R` below 5%** — both screens fail. The current decomposition cannot support the stated
    40	  requirement for C3, and the panel as designed should not be built. That is reported plainly,
    41	  against fable's stated conclusion and astra's, without softening.
    42	
    43	OBJMISMATCH is read the same way on its own half and does not substitute for `R`.
    44	
    45	## What does not count as evidence here
    46	
    47	- Any gain measured under the **capacity** numerator. One such headline moved from `+113.412%`
    48	  to `+0.273%` today when the demand cap was applied.
    49	- Any **oracle-only** gain, including a mode-selection counterfactual that uses the realised
    50	  fading draw.
    51	- Any loss value, from any route, in any direction.
    52	- Anything measured on the shipped surrogate corpus, whose C1/C2 labels are not the declared
    53	  targets.
    54	
    55	## Validity condition, declared in advance
    56	
    57	`EVALPATH` is currently determining whether `StepEvaluator.evaluate` and `evaluate_many`
    58	disagree on the same `Configuration`, and if so which is authoritative. **If it finds that
    59	RESIDTOGGLE was scored through the non-authoritative path, or through a mixture of the two,
    60	that measurement must be repeated on the authoritative path.**
    61	
    62	This repetition is declared **now, before either result is known**, precisely so that it
    63	cannot later be an outcome-selected rerun. It is conditioned on a validity finding about the
    64	instrument, not on the value of `R`. If EVALPATH finds the paths agree, or finds RESIDTOGGLE
    65	used the authoritative path, the first result stands as reported — **including if it fails
    66	the screens**.
    67	
    68	## What I will not do
    69	
    70	- I will not re-run either measurement because of what it reported.
    71	- I will not move a screen, in either direction, after seeing a number.
    72	- I will not report a pass by quoting the more favourable of the two numerators.
    73	- I will not describe a result between the two screens as a pass.
FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-TRAINING-GATE-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Pre-declaration — the gate that must pass before any training run
     2	
     3	**2026-09-10, written BEFORE `FACTORIAL` and `C1REAL` report.** No sealed artefact, constant,
     4	threshold, sign, seed, horizon, price, guard or acceptance rule is changed. This fixes the
     5	condition for starting training while the deciding numbers do not yet exist.
     6	
     7	## The wrong gate, and why I nearly used it
     8	
     9	Earlier today I framed the training gate as: the corpus is real, and the sealed checkpoint
    10	format can express the protocol. Both matter, but **neither is the gate.** The format
    11	question is "can we write it down"; it says nothing about whether writing it down is worth
    12	anything.
    13	
    14	**The gate is the exact ceiling.** Every route's exact marginal is an upper bound on what a
    15	learned head predicting that route can deliver: the exact term hands the selector the true
    16	value, a head hands it an estimate. A route worth `x%` with exact terms is worth **at most**
    17	`x%` with a head, and strictly less whenever the head errs.
    18	
    19	Training before the exact marginals are known would measure a shortfall against an unknown
    20	bound. That is the failure mode recorded earlier today — building a component before building
    21	the contrast that gives it meaning.
    22	
    23	## The gate
    24	
    25	Training may be proposed only when **both** hold, and each is reported before the proposal:
    26	
    27	**G1 — the exact marginals justify it.** `FACTORIAL` (dispatched 08:26 UTC) completes the
    28	`2^3` factorial with exact terms on `FULLSPAN`'s catalogue, anchors, guard, tie-break,
    29	provisioning, price and pooling, reporting `C1_ONLY`, `C2_ONLY`, `C3_ONLY`, the three `DROP`
    30	arms, `FULL` and `BASELINE`, demand-capped. Against the owner's current bar — the three
    31	together substantial, one or two contributing little acceptable — G1 passes when the joint
    32	span is substantial **and** the report states plainly which single-route marginals are
    33	positive and which are not. **No numerical pass mark is invented here; the magnitudes are
    34	reported and the bar is the owner's.**
    35	
    36	**G2 — the target is learnable.** `C1REAL` must show the ceiling on the declared target is
    37	**architectural, not informational**. If a high-capacity model on the same 16 inputs also
    38	fails, the limit is in the information, and no architecture, epoch count or seed repairs it.
    39	**That conclusion is reachable without training and would make training pointless.**
    40	
    41	## What happens under each outcome
    42	
    43	- **G1 and G2 both pass** — propose five production arms, 500 epochs, cadence 100, on the
    44	  exact corpus. That protocol is round-trip verified in the sealed format and resume is
    45	  bit-exact. Its purpose is the one quantity nothing has measured: **how much of the exact
    46	  ceiling a learned head recovers.** It is not the claim.
    47	- **G1 passes, G2 fails** — do not train this decomposition. The targets change first; the two
    48	  candidate replacements are already specified and their comparison metrics are pre-declared
    49	  in `V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-DECOMPOSITION-BAKEOFF-2026-09-10.md`.
    50	- **G1 fails** — do not train. A ceiling that does not justify a head is not repaired by
    51	  fitting one.
    52	- **The residual-sign contradiction still unresolved when G1 reports** — `FACTORIAL`'s `C3`
    53	  marginals are reported with both `RESIDTOGGLE`'s `+5.62%` and `C3REACH`'s `-60%` beside
    54	  them, per the binding rule in
    55	  `V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-CONTRADICTION-RESIDUAL-SIGN-2026-09-10.md`. `SIGNFORK` is the
    56	  discriminating measurement.
    57	
    58	## What this gate is not
    59	
    60	It is not a new scientific gate on any claim. It governs **whether to spend compute**, not
    61	whether any hypothesis is accepted or rejected. No acceptance rule, threshold, sign or
    62	estimand is created, moved or removed by it.
    63	
    64	It also does not authorise contract v2, corpus substitution, or a panel. Those remain
    65	separate and unauthorised.
FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-REQUIREMENT-CHANGE-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Requirement change — the bar moves from three individual gains to the joint span
     2	
     3	**2026-09-10, ~07:00 UTC. Recorded by the controller. This is an owner decision about what
     4	the paper claims, not a change to any estimand, formula, sign, threshold, seed, horizon,
     5	price, guard or acceptance rule. Nothing sealed is modified.**
     6	
     7	## The owner's words
     8	
     9	> "應該是說3個加起來要有明顯的提升，如果真的有1、2個是提升的比較少也只能接受，最好是只有1個
    10	> 或沒有，但是不能3個加起來還提升很少，那就感覺沒什麼意義了"
    11	
    12	**The bar is now `FULL - BASELINE` substantial.** One or two routes contributing little is
    13	acceptable; ideally at most one does. What is not acceptable is all three together amounting
    14	to very little.
    15	
    16	## The sequence, recorded in full because the timing matters
    17	
    18	| When | Bar |
    19	|---|---|
    20	| earlier | each of C1, C2, C3 must individually raise EE; a "C3 negative result" is not acceptable |
    21	| then | the **ordering**: baseline + each of C1/C2/C3 individually positive, and FULL > any pair > control |
    22	| then | "如果只能提升1% 那就沒有什麼意義" — 1% is not a meaningful result |
    23	| then | "不用超過古典搜尋也沒關係" — the full system need not beat classical search |
    24	| **now** | **the three together must be substantial; individual positivity is preferred, not required** |
    25	
    26	**This change was made after `RESIDTOGGLE` reported.** The owner had the residual-ceiling
    27	number, `+5.62%` demand-capped, in hand. I record that plainly.
    28	
    29	It is nonetheless not outcome-selection in the sense the non-negotiables forbid, and the
    30	distinction is worth stating precisely:
    31	
    32	- **What is forbidden** is tuning a formula, sign, threshold, seed, horizon, price or
    33	  acceptance rule against an observed result, or selecting a rerun by its outcome. None of
    34	  those has happened. No estimand has changed; every measurement already taken stands exactly
    35	  as reported, under the reading rule declared before it ran.
    36	- **What changed** is which claim the paper makes. That is the owner's to set, and it was set
    37	  by narrowing an ambition, not by moving a pass mark on a fixed test. The pre-declared 10%
    38	  and 5% screens for the residual **still stand as stated**, and `RESIDTOGGLE` is still
    39	  reported against them: `+5.62%`, below astra's 10%, above fable's 5%, with fable's second
    40	  half still pending.
    41	
    42	I am recording the timing because a reader is entitled to it, not because I think the change
    43	is improper.
    44	
    45	## What this changes in the work
    46	
    47	**Load-bearing before, much less so now:**
    48	- Whether C3 alone clears a screen. It is now a component of a span, not a gate.
    49	- Whether each route can independently change a committed decision. Still worth knowing —
    50	  `C3REACH` continues — but no longer decisive.
    51	- The panel spine's move set (erratum 16). Still a real design defect that must be re-declared
    52	  before any panel, but it no longer determines whether the claim survives.
    53	
    54	**Load-bearing now:**
    55	- **`FULL - BASELINE` on the reported numerator.** Not measured. `FULLSPAN` dispatched at
    56	  07:01 UTC to measure it on `RESIDTOGGLE`'s own catalogue, anchors, guard, tie-break,
    57	  provisioning and pooling, adding only the committed nearest-eligible incumbent as a third
    58	  selector, so the span decomposes as
    59	  `BASELINE -> ADDITIVE_ONLY -> WITH_RESIDUAL`.
    60	- The **exact/oracle-to-learned gap**. Every span measured this way is a **ceiling**: it hands
    61	  the selector exact terms rather than predictions. What learned heads recover from that
    62	  ceiling is a separate measurement and must never be conflated with it.
    63	- Whether the corpus can carry the declared targets at all (`EXACTGEN`, `C1REAL`).
    64	
    65	**Unchanged:**
    66	- `ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL` is never relabelled `BASELINE`. The span's reference is the committed
    67	  nearest-eligible incumbent; the all-neutral arm is a different object and keeps its name.
    68	- No TEST split. No tuning against results. No outcome-selected rerun. Sealed artefacts and
    69	  frozen manifests are not rewritten.
    70	- Every finding recorded today stands unchanged, including the ones that make the work harder.
