FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-STATUS-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Controller status — end of 2026-09-10
     2	A single readable state of the project. Every number below has a receipt in a dated record in this directory. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM` throughout: nothing sealed was modified today except one false provenance comment, and no training or policy run was authorised.
     3	
     4	## The owner's requirement, stated exactly
     5	Each of the three learned routes must individually raise pooled energy efficiency, and the ordering must hold: full system above any two, any two above the control. Magnitudes need not add.
     6	
     7	This is **contract §C3**, the neutral-source substitution contrast: for a named route, its training source is replaced by a neutral one while all heads are retained, updated and deployed. It is **not** §C4, which the contract itself heads *coordination attribution, beyond the source claim*. I conflated the two all day; that is erratum 14.
     8	
     9	**§C3 has never been measured at scale.** The only run touching it was a two-seed, one-world, five-anchor pilot in which six of ten decisions fell outside the training support.
    10	
    11	## The five decisions
    12	| | decision | state |
    13	|---|---|---|
    14	| 1 | correct the provisioning rule | **blocked on framing.** The numerical blocker is discharged; the remaining objection stands: v1.9 §1 says in terms that the margin must not be re-solved into transmit power, and v1.1 calls the rate figure nominal and permits partial delivery. It may proceed only as an explicitly declared **policy change**, with the rationale independent of what it does to any route's sign. |
    15	| 2 | beam-width convention | **tied to 1.** The adjudication requires the sealed width frozen for the provisioning comparison, with any antenna change given its own separate decision. |
    16	| 3 | open the contract for direct prediction | **closed: no.** It removes the three-route structure the requirement is stated over. |
    17	| 4 | promote the deadline comparator | **closed: no.** A competent anytime unilateral already holds 81.7 % and 87.9 % of its converged gain at the 30.08-second interval. |
    18	| 5 | add three single-informative-route arms | **pending the tier verification now running.** |
    19	
    20	## The corrected-physics coordination picture
    21	| panel | pairing | span |
    22	|---|---|---:|
    23	| twenty anchors | **correct** | **+1.2913 %**, 1/20 negative |
    24	| thirty dates | old | +0.717 %, CI [+0.436 %, +0.997 %], 4/30 negative |
    25	| five widths, strict numerics | old | −0.1768 % at the sealed width, +2.3460 % at the source's width |
    26	
    27	Small, positive, with a lower interval edge approaching immateriality. Three routes must each show a resolvable positive marginal — but the marginals are **not** bounded by this band, because a leave-one-out arm can select worse than its fallback, and the owner's bar is an ordering rather than a per-contrast threshold.
    28	
    29	Every exploratory route on the coordination side is closed: the deadline route, the prefix-removal route (seeding from raw geometry recovers 5–6 % of the prefix's uplift), and the reparametrisation route.
    30	
    31	## What is known about each route
    32	**First route — the bottleneck.** Held-out `R² 0.151`, pairwise ordering `0.650`; 79.3 % of target variance sits in whole-network coupled terms and 98.9 % of the externality is within-anchor so none cancels in ranking. An oracle removing only the cross-user externality reaches `0.902`. Verdict `TARGET_REFORMULATE`. Ridge reaches EV `+0.089`, positive on 10/10 leave-one-step-out folds; collision-bound variance is **zero**. The one admissible feature found bought exactly nothing because it is constant at all thirty anchors. A test of the cheapest remaining repair — giving it the resource context the interaction head already consumes — is running.
    33	
    34	**Second route — best posed.** Target verdict `TARGET_WELL_POSED`; its reviewer explicitly declined to redesign it. Ridge EV `+0.301`, positive on 8/8 folds. **But its stored survival flags are wrong on 822 of 1,784 rows** through an adapter that writes geometric legality into both the validity and survival fields. That repair is owed and has not been made.
    35	
    36	**Third route — its named threat is refuted.** Learned interaction head 3.618 mean selection regret against a size-only prior's 13.114 and zero's 13.683: knowing the coalition size is worth 0.569, the learned head is worth 9.496. Its decision-level justification is the exact-pair replay: pairwise truncation reverses the winner at 27.8 % of anchors, 92 % of those beyond the project's margin.
    37	
    38	## Execution order from here
    39	1. finish the four running jobs;
    40	2. repair the second route's adapter defect;
    41	3. draft the provisioning **policy-change declaration** if decision 1 proceeds, on the adjudication's stated conditions;
    42	4. build the §C3 panel on whatever tier the verification says is sound, with a degeneracy screen that disqualifies any arm sitting below the certified fixed point before any ordering is read;
    43	5. **run §C3.** This is where the owner's question is answered for the first time.
    44	
    45	## My estimate
    46	Roughly 3 to 3.5 in 10, with the first route as the binding constraint. Composition matters more than the number: the third route improved today, the second is best-posed but needs its adapter fixed, and the first has no known path until the running test reports.
    47	
    48	## The methodological record
    49	Eighteen corrections today, listed in the errata records. **Not one was caught by my own review**; each came from adversarial review, independent replication, external reading, or the owner. Twice I rebuilt a case against a sealed declaration that a prior adversarial review had already rejected.
    50	
    51	The rule that follows, and that I have written into memory: **a controller claim sourced from one model, one panel, or one intermediate file is a hypothesis until an independent line confirms it.** The findings that survived the day all have two independent sources.
FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-STRATEGIC-ENERGY-IS-IN-THE-CONTROL-LAW-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Controller strategic observation — the energy is in the control law, not in the association
     2	Recorded 2026-09-10 after the owner said plainly that a one per cent improvement is not a meaningful result and asked for a direction that genuinely raises efficiency. This is **reasoning over today's measurements, not a new measurement**, and it is recorded as a direction to be decided, not started. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`.
     3	
     4	## The arithmetic that settles where the leverage is
     5	The power amplifier accounts for **94.8 %** of consumed power, and its draw is set by the **power and mode control law** — not by which user is attached to which beam.
     6	
     7	| what moved | pooled efficiency |
     8	|---|---|
     9	| **correcting one defect in the control law** | **28.47 → 43.71, about +53 %** |
    10	| everything the association layer can contend for — coordination, joint search, all three learned routes | **about +1 %** |
    11	
    12	**The largest efficiency movement measured today came from a control-law repair, not from any association decision.** And that repair only removed a defect; nobody has asked whether the law is well designed.
    13	
    14	## Why the association layer is limited to about one per cent
    15	It is not a weakness of the algorithm. Association decisions simply do not move much energy. Two local optima of the association search differ by about eight per cent; the coordinated optimum sits about one per cent above the certified fixed point. Both are small because they rearrange *who attaches where* while the energy is spent on *how much power each beam radiates and in which mode*.
    16	
    17	**The project has been looking for energy where the energy is not.**
    18	
    19	## This was predicted this morning and I did not act on it
    20	The strategic review's closing section asked whether the occupancy-induced blackout should exist at all, proposed comparing a service-aware power and mode policy against the existing law, and said: *if much of the coordination gain disappears, the contribution becomes a diagnosis of the control law and its remedy — possibly more useful than teaching three networks to compensate for it.*
    21	
    22	**That condition came true.** Correcting the provisioning took the coordination gain from 6.36 % to about 1 %. I spent the remaining hours pursuing the one per cent.
    23	
    24	## The option, stated with its costs
    25	The three-route structure survives a change of decision object. Pointed at the control law rather than the association, the roles map directly: the surplus of changing a beam's power and mode setting; whether that setting persists; and the interaction between beams' settings. **The interaction is stronger there**, because power settings couple directly through interference rather than indirectly through shared airtime, so the third route would have more to predict, not less.
    26	
    27	Three honest qualifications:
    28	1. **The +53 % was a defect repair, not an algorithmic gain.** It demonstrates that the control law has high leverage — a single defect there cost more than the entire association layer can win — but it is **not** fifty-three per cent sitting available.
    29	2. **The control law's improvable margin has never been measured**, exactly as the association layer's one per cent had never been measured before today.
    30	3. **It is a large pivot**: targets, heads and three contract sections would be rewritten.
    31	
    32	## What should happen before any decision
    33	The screening run is already committed and its cost already spent. It answers whether the three-head architecture functions at all, and that knowledge transfers to any decision object.
    34	
    35	Beside it, one measurement would answer the owner's question directly: **how far is the current power and mode control law from the best achievable, on the same panels?** That is the control-law analogue of the multi-start ceiling now being measured for the association layer, and nobody has ever asked it.
    36	
    37	**Proposed, not started.** The owner was told the reason it is necessary rather than merely interesting, and the decision is theirs.
FILE controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-STRATEGIC-REFRAMING-2026-09-10.md
     1	# Controller record — two independent strategic reviews reached the same verdict, and it is not the one I was working toward
     2	Recorded 2026-09-10. Two reviews were commissioned with fresh context on different model families, given the same prompt, and explicitly told to question the frame rather than the details. They did not see each other's work.
     3	
     4	## The verdict, in their own words
     5	* One: "**The mechanism is the paper; the learned coordinator is an unproven follow-on project and should stop determining this paper's scope.**"
     6	* The other: "**The mechanism is the contribution. The learned coordinator is not, and on the evidence already in hand it is not going to become one on this timeline.**"
     7	
     8	Both are scoped to **this paper and this timeline**. Neither says the three-component goal is wrong or unreachable.
     9	
    10	## The sentence that indicts my day
    11	> The controller has treated today's discoveries as reasons to **repair** the original research programme. They are stronger reasons to **replace its primary question**.
    12	
    13	That is accurate. I read every finding as "what to fix". Collectively they say "what to ask instead".
    14	
    15	## What the reframed paper contains, and five of six parts are already measured
    16	1. **Mechanism.** Under a rate target with equal-airtime multiplexing and adaptive coding, raising beam occupancy enlarges back-off room so a lower mode clears its threshold. Adding load to a beam can make it servable. Four constructive witnesses through the production scoring path, plus a reuse-colour control that drives the interaction to −5.9e−6 bits and isolates interference as necessary in one of them.
    17	2. **Prevalence.** Qualifying coalitions at 30 of 30 real anchors, median energy-efficiency gain 9.118 %, range 4.156 to 22.756 %. Occupancy activation 28/30, complete beam evacuation 29/30, multi-aggressor relief **0/30**. About 61 % of active beam-anchor incidences sit at occupancy 1 or 2, the regime that delivers nothing.
    18	3. **Ceiling.** A perfect-knowledge bounded set selector beats an exhaustively certified unilateral optimum by **+6.359 %** pooled energy efficiency over 20 anchors with served counts **up**, 1,957 against 1,939 against 826, robust across 18 circuit-accounting combinations at +4.84 % to +6.59 % and **larger at zero per-chain power**, the architecture an outside hardware review called fatal.
    19	4. **Structure.** The interaction is a threshold on summed occupancy and the pairwise decomposition is measurably misspecified, with the third-and-above remainder exceeding 1e−3 on 38.50 % of 5,003 coalitions.
    20	5. **Unreachability, which is what makes the paper matter.** The certified unilateral comparator needs up to 1,213 s against a 10 s budget, 91.55 % of it in irreducible coupled-power solves; iteration counts are bimodal at {0, 46, 50, 80, 86, 86} with nothing between 1 and 45, so no realistic budget increase converts an anchor; and the engine admits **no valid pruning certificate** because the hard decode thresholds defeat any Lipschitz enclosure. **Real headroom exists that exhaustive search cannot reach in budget.** That converts the motivation for approximate coordination from an assumption into a measurement.
    21	6. **A negative result reported as one.** The learned interaction head does not beat a constant-zero predictor on realised efficiency, with item 4 as the diagnosis.
    22	
    23	## The weakest point, named precisely: N
    24	Every number above comes from one to four worlds, two dates, one constellation, 20 to 30 anchors. **There is no interval on the +6.36 %.** A referee asks for the distribution over geometries and there is nothing.
    25	
    26	It is also the cheapest item on the board. The prior ceiling run took 694.6 s for 20 anchors on four processes, and the diagnostic is **learner-free**, so the contested train-versus-evaluation date-boundary question does not apply to it at all. Thirty dates at 20 anchors is single-digit core-hours. That measurement is now running.
    27	
    28	I had been treating the date shortage as one large blocker. It is two separate problems and only the learner-side one is hard.
    29	
    30	## Two frames I had not considered
    31	**Nobody has measured the one-line policy.** The mechanism is a property of a **beam**, not of a coalition: no beam below occupancy three, consolidate or empty. What fraction of the +6.36 % that captures has never been measured, and both answers are valuable. If it captures most, a sub-millisecond physically motivated rule beats an exhaustive optimiser and the learner question retires. If it captures little, the coordination structure is demonstrably non-trivial, which the project currently asserts rather than shows. Now running.
    32	
    33	**The objective may be the wrong one, and 0/30 is the tell.** With quality of service as a guard rather than an outcome, the optimiser has no reason to spread load ever. Reporting an efficiency-against-worst-decile-rate frontier would be a stronger claim, and the served counts rising rather than falling suggest **we may already have the stronger version and be reporting the weaker one**.
    34	
    35	## Architecture, measured while the reviews ran
    36	Both alternatives beat the pairwise baseline on selection regret, and the resource-aware form leads on exactly the population the pairwise form cannot represent.
    37	
    38	| model | mean regret, all | mean regret, material remainder | exact-best, material remainder |
    39	|---|---:|---:|---:|
    40	| pairwise baseline | 7.00 | 4.74 | 19.4 % |
    41	| resource anchored | 5.68 | **3.22** | 26.1 % |
    42	| same-anchor ranker | **5.25** | 3.53 | **31.7 %** |
    43	
    44	The resource-aware model also selects three-member coalitions 115 times against the pairwise model's 57, and the verified mechanism needs exactly three. Best exact-best rate is still only 31.7 %, so better is not yet good.
    45	
    46	## Standing
    47	No threshold, sign, seed, horizon, price, service guard, acceptance rule or claim condition changes. No run is authorised. Whether to adopt the reframing is the owner's decision; these are two reviewers' recommendations and the measurements that support them.

