   135	## Owed-repair register — no repair performed
   136	
   137	1. Owners must declare separate authority for held-snapshot selection and full-trajectory committed physics, or declare one API contract that both methods implement.
   138	2. Make cache identity include evaluation semantics (at least field and boundary policy), or reject attempts to mix population methods in one evaluator.
   139	3. Add real-configuration parity tests for `(0,)`, full-48 nominal and realised fields, and ACM threshold-edge rows. Require the intended equality/tolerance explicitly.
   140	4. After authority is settled, regenerate or invalidate primitive coalition rows and rerun pilot S0/S_UNI/exact-interaction diagnostics. Audit downstream selections before interpreting any EE outcome.
   141	5. Add a real evaluator to Stage-C acceptance coverage so receipt provenance establishes which physical path produced bits and joules.
   142	
   143	Until those decisions and reruns occur, existing claims are not automatically false, but mixed-path selection/coalition evidence is not claim-grade.

