    45	
    46	**Mostly no, on these two anchors.** An independent local probe—each beam choosing from the same grid using its own decoded rate and PA/chain cost while holding other beams at their declared powers—reached **94.796 Mbit/J** pooled, +108.915% over the declared law and only **2.107% below** the coupled search's 96.836 Mbit/J. The large gain therefore looks predominantly per-beam-local; exact cross-beam information appears useful for the last roughly two per cent, not for the main effect. This is a rough two-anchor judgement, not a proof.
