+| 7 | “The large full-minus-drop result proves useful three-route design.” | Neutral-arm collapse, source intervention confused with knockout, or post-treatment filtering. | **20–40 min, arithmetic only:** compare FULL, all-neutral, each drop and an independent strong reference on the full scheduled population. Print their absolute bits, energy and EE; label any restricted subset as conditional. Keep source benefit and architecture benefit separate. |
+| 8 | “The exact pipeline costs 29.42 hours and training can start on that projection.” | Both anchor timings used 992 rows but different execution scope; model inputs, coalition work, legal-action coverage and endpoints are excluded. | **20–40 min, no timing run:** reconcile existing work counters, switches, tape sizes, fields and boundaries for 49.03 and 632.83 seconds. Cost the actual proposed protocol as separate setup, source, coalition, training and evaluation terms; flag unmeasured terms. |
+| 9 | “Positive counts settle service and substantiality.” | At-least-one-decode service, individual losers, small date count and an unfixed practical bar. | **15–30 min, existing ledger:** retain 39/800 losses and attainment alongside pooled gain; reconcile 6/20 versus 1/20; list unique dates and reused carriers. Specify the practical decision criterion prospectively, not by choosing among observed headline percentages. |
+
+**Prospective reading rules for the five pending measurements.**
+
+These rules interpret results; they do not authorize runs or alter the existing experiment. If a job has already completed, the rules remain prospective to my reading because I have not opened its output. A validity failure should be reported as such, preserving the original result; it is not permission to hunt for a favourable rerun.
+
+**OBJMISMATCH.** A legal single-user move improving capped committed EE disproves the relevant endpoint's local optimality **for that objective and neighbourhood**. It does not invalidate its old fixed-price certificate. Count all tested endpoints, the number with improving moves, and the attainable reported gain, with bits, joules and guard semantics. A high flip rate with negligible gain means mismatch without demonstrated practical importance. A small number of large gains means concentrated opportunity, not universal failure.
+
+A complete negative census establishes local optimality only on the tested legal singleton neighbourhood. A sampled negative result means “none found.” Neither excludes other starts, swaps or coordinated controls. Also distinguish per-anchor ratio optimization from whole-panel ratio optimization. With positive energy, a candidate improves the panel when `ΔN−eta_panel*ΔE>0`, where `eta_panel` is the current pooled ratio. Testing against each anchor's own eta answers a different question. A hindsight gain does not establish causal recoverability, C1 learnability, or that merely changing eta resolves the snapshot-versus-horizon mismatch.
+
+**C1REAL.** First authenticate the exact target, physical lineage, feature values and split. “Same 16 inputs” must mean the same deployable information, not simply 16 slots populated by a more expensive evaluator. A strong held-out predictor on those admissible inputs demonstrates predictability on that support and weakens an architectural explanation tied to the smaller model. Good within-user ordering but poor catalogue top choice indicates that composition or cross-user scale remains a problem; good value prediction alone settles neither.
+
+Failure of all tested estimators leaves the architectural-versus-informational cause **UNDETERMINED** unless there is additional identification evidence. Exact same-input/different-target cases prove ambiguity for those cases; quantify their mass and whether they reverse relevant decisions. Absence of observed collisions does not prove sufficiency. A model that succeeds only after reading coupled candidate outcomes establishes an oracle-feature result. Under no outcome should R², loss or ordering be restated as an EE gain. Under no outcome does target predictability alone prove the benefit of informative-source training.
+
+**EXACTGEN.** A pass means a specified set of rows faithfully implements a specified target and input contract, with authenticated source, fields, boundary grids, references, prices, Phi and three-offset semantics. It does not mean that a flag change alone repaired the deployed inference path. Require baseline/self-action identities and same-path base/singleton/joint construction; verify numerical units and the difference between exact arithmetic over binary64 receipts and exact physical truth. A zero algebraic identity residual cannot authenticate the semantics of its operands.
+
+Report row inclusion and coalition coverage, including empty/singleton handling, grand rows and missing sizes; legality filtering can change the training population. Separate target generation from inference-feature acquisition. For cost reconciliation, equal row counts do not imply equal work. If 49.03 and 632.83 seconds are reconciled by boundary count, optional coalition work or execution settings, state that mechanism and scope the rate accordingly. If not, cost is **UNDETERMINED**, not “affordable because one receipt says so.” Partial completion is an exact partial corpus, not a completed corpus. A complete corpus is readiness evidence, never EE evidence.
+
+**SIGNFORK.** Require all four cells to share physical world, anchor set, action catalogue, candidate outcomes, additive background, residual definition and guard, except the two named factors. Print the two price effects separately at each gate setting and the two gate effects separately at each price setting; do not describe an averaged effect as universal if the interaction is large. Changes must be in committed reported bits/energy, not only argmax or surrogate score.
+
+If changing price helps under both gates, that supports a price effect **in that fixed experiment**. If the gate matters under both prices, inspect which formerly zero/missing rows changed and whether the intervention replaced the residual object. If only their combination helps, the interpretation is an interaction; neither factor alone is the explanation. If neither matters, the contradiction remains unresolved; learned-versus-exact additive background, horizon mixing, catalogue and physical lineage remain candidates. If the exact residual is zero wherever contexts are absent, a null gate effect is expected algebraically and says nothing about the learned head's scale.
+
+Do not call a favourable cell a new operating rule. Do not assert that one world's four cells reconcile the two original reports unless you can transport their score definitions and reproduce each original treatment under the matched construction. Retain +5.62% and the approximately −60% hybrid changed-subset result with their different meanings until that is done.
+
+**FACTORIAL.** Before any sign is read, require eight distinct **factor settings** `000…111`, plus the external nearest-eligible BASELINE as a ninth reference unless an explicit identity establishes coincidence. An exact `000` score may tie-break to a nonbaseline candidate; it is not automatically the trained all-neutral control. Distinguish exact factor removal from neutral-source retraining. Identify how C2 is represented: a genuine three-offset continuation, the sealed oracle tie-break, or an alternative partition of immediate singleton surplus. These are not interchangeable. Under the sealed oracle tie-break, zero C2 effect with a unique primary maximum is expected and is not evidence that learned Q2 cannot help proposals.
+
+For each route report standalone benefit `eta({i})−eta(000)` and conditional benefit `eta(111)−eta(111\{i})`, plus full versus external baseline, each with an explicit relative denominator when expressed as a percentage. A factorial interaction is a difference of those effects on a chosen scale, not the physical Ψ. If prices are re-optimized per cell, the results are whole-procedure effects including re-pricing; if fixed, name the common price. A full exact score must reconstruct the intended objective before it can supply any upper bound.
+
+A large full span with small singles can mean complementarity; a large full span with one dominant single may satisfy the owner's revised goal while providing little reason for the other routes. Large leave-one-out effects with weak full-versus-strong-reference performance indicate dependence within this design, not a strong design. A small full span bounds the fixed catalogue's opportunity only if FULL really is its reported-objective optimum under the same constraints. It does not prove all decompositions, catalogues or causal policies futile. A negative residual marginal in a fixed-price proxy factorial need not be impossible; a full optimum losing to another cell under the identical reporting objective and feasible catalogue demands a semantics/optimization reconciliation.
+
+Finally, a positive exact factorial does **not** pass a learned-source claim or demonstrate learnability. Under the owner's revised goal, report magnitudes without inventing a numerical “substantial” threshold after seeing them. If no prospective practical threshold exists, the mechanical G1 pass/fail is **UNDETERMINED** and the result is a planning input. This is a limit on the conclusion, not a reason to commission another open-ended audit cycle.
+
+The records already contain enough information to prevent the next fake success metric. The missing action is to bind each conclusion to the intervention that actually produced its number, before using it to decide what should be trained.
+
