+
+**Q2 — Load-bearing premises that remain wrong or unverified.**
+
+**A. “The exact path repairs the data while preserving the inputs needed by a cheap predictor.” Wrong. V-code/V-receipt.** The [exact builder, lines 599–672][exactinputs] fills Q1 features from the candidate's evaluated margin, required power and ACM efficiency; Q2 features include evaluated future projections. [The cost receipt][rowcost] identifies those suppliers explicitly. The [data census][census] finds all Q1 and Q2 state vectors differ across the two paths at both diffed anchors. Switching paths changes features as well as labels, despite retaining the same dimensional schema. Some feature acquisition requires the very candidate solve the head is supposed to avoid. That may be allowed in an offline teacher; it is not free inference. The deployment feature supplier and its cost remain **UNDETERMINED** for the proposed successor.
+
+**B. “Failure of a high-capacity model proves an informational ceiling.” Wrong. D.** The training gate G2 and [bakeoff metric 3][bakeoff] assert this. Finite-sample failure can arise from estimation, optimization, regularization, distribution shift, scaling or the tested model family. A collision witness can prove non-identifiability for those states; a validated distributional lower bound can quantify its prevalence. A failed fit cannot. Success would establish useful predictability on that held-out support, not a universal architectural diagnosis. The gate turns an inconclusive result into an impossibility proof and can stop useful work for the wrong reason.
+
+**C. “Missing contexts restrict C3 to changing about one fifth of catalogues/decisions.” Wrong as a frequency bound. V-code/D.** [Pilot lines 1509–1515][pilotcontexts] create contexts for every legal row with at least two changed users. The missing rows are the empty/singleton case under that rule. Their mutual scores cannot change, but **one** altered multi-user row can overtake every singleton at every anchor. A 79% row share gives no 21% bound on decision reachability. C3REACH's exact branch applies exact Ψ to **all** legal rows; the context gate is explicitly on the learned branch. A gate fork on an exact residual that is correctly zero for empty/singleton sets should be a no-op unless the factor changes something else.
+
+**D. “The residual sign is primarily a price-versus-context question.” Incomplete. V-code.** Learned versus exact additive background and mixed-horizon residual construction are missing from the declared causal story. The open-contradiction record also says a price explanation would be repairable “without touching any of the three routes.” That does not follow: C1 and Ψ are price-dependent targets. Changing eta changes labels, scale and potentially training, even if the architecture stays fixed.
+
+**E. “There is one head-independent certified fixed point, hence a universal floor and degeneracy test.” Conditional, then overextended. D/V-record.** A deterministic algorithm with fixed initial state, ordering, objective and guard has one reproducible output. Head independence alone does not specify those ingredients, and your arm-owned-seed design changes an ingredient. The certified reference can be common only by an explicit separate construction. More seriously, [the degeneracy screen][degeneracy] conditions on **every compared arm's observed performance** exceeding the reference. Its restricted estimate describes a selected successful subset, not an unbiased source effect. Printing the all-anchor result beside it makes the selection visible; it does not make it causal. A neutral arm's worse performance can be a real source-training effect while still failing to justify the whole architecture against a strong baseline.
+
+**F. “A trained full/drop comparison, an exact-term knockout and a physical interaction are interchangeable.” Wrong. V-record/D.** Your erratum 14 separates these; the training gate merges them again. A fixed-model output knockout, a retrained neutral-source substitution, and a different exact optimizer are three interventions. The physical identity `Ψ(A)=ΔF(A)−Σd_i` is not the statistical interaction of the eight training-source cells. Likewise, single-route benefit versus all-neutral is not single-route benefit versus raw geometry.
+
+**G. “The certified unilateral endpoint is a Nash equilibrium and the bounded gap is price of anarchy.” Unsupported as stated.** [TERMINOLOGY][terminology] supplies neither a game with players' payoffs and feasible deviations nor a worst-equilibrium/global-social-optimum comparison. The code searches a common guarded network objective. One could define an identical-interest constrained game around it, but that is an additional modelling statement. A bounded candidate maximum versus one endpoint is not a price-of-anarchy estimate. The accompanying “few per cent is typical” does not establish this system's limit. Use “this search's local endpoint and its bounded joint extension.”
+
+**H. “Energy is set by the control law, not association; interaction is stronger at the power object; mode control is orthogonal to the decomposition.” Unsupported. D.** A law maps state and assignment into powers. Fixing the law does not fix energy across assignments. Nor does a stronger coupling coefficient prove greater decision value for a residual head. Mode changes alter credited bits, the usefulness of assignments and their interactions, so they are not quantitatively orthogonal interventions. The strategic-energy record and bakeoff silently assume this transfer.
+
+**I. “The exact corpus costs 49.03 seconds per anchor; the discrepant 632.83 seconds used different row densities.” First is partial; second is contradicted by the receipts. V-receipt.** Both reports measured **992 rows**. The 49.03-second benchmark excluded coalition construction, full legal-action enumeration, tape setup, training and endpoints; its two anchors are two carriers of the **same physical step**. The 632.83-second report also says 992 rows. Different execution work or configuration may explain the difference, but row density has not. `AFFORDABLE` applies to the scoped source-row component, not the training programme. EXACTGEN must reconcile actual work counters and settings before either rate is extrapolated.
+
+**J. “Predeclared means statistically unselected; unchanged numbers mean the estimand is unchanged.” Wrong. V-record/D.** The [requirement change][requirement] openly occurred after +5.62% was seen. The owner is entitled to change the goal. That creates an exploratory new claim and changes what success means, even if no number is recomputed. “Substantial” has no numerical decision rule, so G1 is not a determinate pass/fail test yet. Similarly, keeping the existing beam width because it was the “most stable point sampled” is an outcome-based justification for retention. Keeping a previously fixed value is defensible; claiming the exposure to favourable-antenna selection “disappears entirely” is not. Do not repair this by picking a fresh threshold from the same results.
+
+**K. “Two independent reviewers establish the premise.” Wrong.** Reviewer independence is not evidence independence when both consume your same false selector statement or the same receipt. The state says every surviving finding has two sources; the calibration history demonstrates that this is insufficient. For execution claims, identify the executed entry point and imported source, then connect it to the receipt. I checked SHA-256 for the pilot selector, residual-toggle runner and mode-causal script; all three match the hashes printed in their reports. That authenticates the inspected files, not every assertion made about them.
+
+Other categorical claims should be demoted, without commissioning another broad measurement campaign:
+
+- Small correlation with satellite count does not prove the date variation is “not constellation growth”; a single-month panel does not isolate geometry completely. Near-zero rank correlation does not make every prediction using the old rule worthless.
+- The failed load sweep closes that sampled hypothesis, not every coordination direction. An anytime comparator recovering 82–88% of its own gain does not prove no faster learned method could improve the remaining portion.
+- “All earlier learnability evidence used surrogates” contradicts the exact-target 0.151 diagnostic cited in the same corpus finding. Preserve separate provenance, rather than invalidating everything wholesale.
+- A two-arrival occupancy-three witness is a pair interaction. The records repeatedly turn final occupancy three into a requirement for three changed users. Higher-order evidence must come from its own mixed differences/reversals.
+- A 32-pair block plus a summed omitted-pair residual preserves aggregate magnitude, not the identities of all omitted aggressors. “Nothing lost silently” must not become “full pairwise structure retained.”
+- “2 ULP is fixed by IEEE 754” is false. Floating-point format determines ULP spacing, not this algorithm's allowable accumulated error. A 2-ULP gate is a declared engineering tolerance; a 1-ULP discrepancy alone does not prove summation order. Preserve exact identity checks and reason about reduction error separately.
+- The screen's rules “validation still falling means undertrained” and “oscillating means learning rate too high” are diagnoses stated as certainties. Neither curve shape uniquely identifies its cause; neither bears directly on EE.
+- The claim that the mechanism paper is closed on novelty is **UNDETERMINED** here. I did not independently audit the cited literature. The records' twelve-paper inventory cannot settle all publishable questions, and their own assertions about full-buffer versus demand-limited conventions conflict. A claim-by-claim primary-source comparison would settle novelty; reviewer preference cannot.
+- Your score/Phi adjudication left `network_objective` unresolved. I opened [its body, lines 130–144][objective]: it returns `bits − eta*joules`, without Phi. That narrow open question is settled by code; it does not authenticate every caller's composite score.
+
+**Q3 — The three-route structure is not established as the right scientific object.**
+
+**I.** The measured EE story is presently dominated by **search and control-policy choices whose gains have not been attributed to the three catfish sources**. That is the honest answer to the owner's concern. It is not a proof that the physics prohibits three useful heads. The available measurements simply do not select this decomposition over alternatives.
+
+Even the premise “headroom sits outside the heads” needs qualification. Assignment search is a plausible consumer of learned guidance, and temporal CQI makes persistence potentially useful. Those are hypotheses about a new consumer or observation model, not evidence that the present targets and deployment have the right interfaces. The `9.87%` and `+78%` cannot rank research directions quantitatively: they use different reference quality, provisioning, information and candidate restrictions. FULLSPAN itself crosses the association/control boundary you are using to separate those directions.
+
+Your newer requirement removes the argument used to close direct prediction: preserving three individually positive routes is no longer the scientific test. The owner still wants a three-route design, but that is an architectural preference until the contributions or practical advantages are demonstrated. Three numbers that sum exactly are an accounting decomposition; they are not automatically three separately learnable sources or three necessary modules.
+
+The bakeoff's proposed information partition has another unresolved dependency: conditional expectations `E[Y|I]` are population objects, not exact per-row quantities supplied by the physics evaluator. Evaluating that candidate requires a distribution and an estimation procedure. “Offline, with no training” cannot by itself deliver the stipulated held-out model comparisons. Target correlation also does not prove independent information sources, and low correlation does not guarantee useful separate decisions.
+
+The paper can presently support a **model-conditional diagnostic account**: which objective, information and control conventions create the apparent association opportunity; how much finite catalogue hindsight improvement exists; and where a declared causal feedback rule improves same-power credited delivery on the measured tape. Novelty and external validity remain to be established. It cannot currently claim three successful catfish routes or operational energy savings.
+
+A subsequent positive paper could claim **a specified causal controller reaches a stated fraction of a bounded reference's quality at a measured end-to-end cost**, with service distributions and out-of-development evaluation; or **informative source training improves a named controller over its neutral-source version**. Those are different claims and can coexist. Neither requires pretending the exact factorial is a learned-source experiment. A cheap deterministic control rule can be a valuable result if it explains and removes the dominant waste; the number of neural heads is not the contribution by itself.
+
+The fastest defensible route to training is to stop making the measurements decide questions they do not identify. Fix one written mapping from intended observation → features → targets → candidate actions → score → guard → reported endpoint, using the already available code and receipts. Name the new current claim and its reference. Then a bounded learned pilot can answer a learned question. Do not wait for a finite fit to prove an informational theorem, and do not use a positive oracle factorial as proof that the mapping already exists.
+
+**Q4 — Ranked predictions of the next overturning, with checks below one hour.**
+
+These are proposed checks, not runs I performed. Each uses already declared contrasts or audits the existing evidence; none selects a rerun by a favourable outcome. Times are human-work estimates for bounded inspection/arithmetic, not measured runtime promises.
+
+| Rank | Claim most likely to fall next | Mechanism | Cheapest concrete check |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | “FACTORIAL measures the exact contributions of our C1/C2/C3.” | FULLSPAN has one exact singleton term and a residual, with different controls, horizon, guard and price from the heads. A third factor can be invented merely by naming an algebraic split C2. | **20–40 min, no physics:** write each factorial factor as a formula and identify its target function, offset set, units and selector use. Require the full cell to reconstruct the intended score and distinguish `000` from external BASELINE. If no identity connects a factor to declared C2, report an alternative decomposition. |
+| 2 | “SIGNFORK has resolved the residual contradiction.” | Hybrid learned/exact background and mixed-horizon Ψ remain even after a price×gate fork. The exact gate may be mathematically inert. | **20–40 min, no physics:** compare the two existing score-construction paths line by line; audit cached base/singleton/joint field and boundary identities, and whether a gate changes only empty/singleton zeros. Reconcile full/additive score identities before interpreting the fork. |
+| 3 | “C1REAL found an information ceiling” or “EXACTGEN made the model deployable.” | Finite estimator failure is not non-identifiability; exact features may require candidate solves or differ from runtime inputs. | **30–45 min, no fitting:** inspect feature suppliers and archived train/held-out definitions, target lineage, duplicate groups, scaling and availability. Tabulate each of the 16 inputs' acquisition path and online cost. A proved collision bounds only its supported population. |
