+**Your training gate treats oracle contrasts from a different decision problem as upper bounds on the contribution of the declared three learned routes.**
+
+This is an audit of your reasoning. I read the 90 controller records and traced the consequential claims into the worker reports and source identified below. I ran no measurements, fits, optimization searches or simulations. I used one `nice -n 15 /usr/bin/python3` process for arithmetic on printed numbers. I did not access `/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover` or its virtual environment. This report is the only file I created or changed.
+
+Evidence labels: **V-code** means source I opened; **V-receipt** means a worker receipt/report I opened, not an independently repeated experiment; **D** means a derivation; **I** means an inference. A controller record proves that you asserted something, not that it happened. I kept `OBJMISMATCH`, `C1REAL`, `EXACTGEN`, `SIGNFORK` and `FACTORIAL` outputs unopened, including any report file that appeared during this audit. Their reading rules below therefore do not depend on their results.
+
+The error in the first sentence has two independently checkable parts. Your [training gate, lines 14–17][gate] says an exact route marginal is an upper bound on a learned marginal, “strictly less whenever the head errs.” That is false in general. And `FULLSPAN`'s additive scorer is not the declared C1/C2 pair: it sums exact realised singleton changes over association **and power/mode controls**, then solves its own pooled surrogate ratio. Its full scorer optimizes realised outcomes with hindsight. Calling these “exact terms” does not make them exact implementations of your three heads.
+
+You have already recorded the evidence against your gate: [PARAMETRISATION][param] reports that replacing either learned half by its exact counterpart worsens selection regret, from 3.618 to 9.043 or 9.647. This is evidence about ranking, not EE. It is nevertheless directly contrary to the monotonic “more exact component means better decision” premise you subsequently installed as a compute gate. Your own stages 6–8 contract amendment v1.2, item 3, also explicitly allows a learned selector to improve realised EE under model mismatch while remaining bounded by the exact selector on their common selection score.
+
+**Q1 — The evidence ledger, ranked by damage.**
+
+The arithmetic is usually the least troublesome part. The main failure is carrying a number across a change in decision object, information, reference, target, or population without carrying that change with it.
+
+| Rank | Number you are carrying | What it actually measures | What it cannot establish |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | `FULLSPAN +17.03%`; additive `+10.80%` | Eight-anchor, corrected-provisioning, hindsight catalogue comparison against an unsearched nearest-eligible incumbent. Full EE is 9.029226 versus 7.715422 Mbit/J. Additive is 8.548697. | Benefit, learnability, necessity, or attainable gain of the declared three learned heads; benefit over a competent search baseline. |
+| 2 | `RESIDTOGGLE +5.62%` | Full exact pooled-EE optimization versus a singleton-additive surrogate optimizer, with a separate optimized price for each arm. Same expanded catalogue and realised service filter. | The maximum possible C3 source-training effect; a clean fixed-price residual toggle in the deployed pilot. |
+| 3 | `C3REACH 30.82 → 12.30 Mbit/J`, approximately `−60.09%` | Adding an “exact” residual to **learned** additive scores, pooled over the 48 changed anchor-seed decisions. The upstream pilot evaluator has a documented mixed-boundary problem. | A negative full-exact-system result directly contradicting `FULLSPAN`, or proof that interaction itself hurts EE. |
+| 4 | Causal mode selection `+78.02%`, `+76.64%` | Fixed-power re-crediting on one world, four anchors, using exact one-boundary-old simulated SINR; failures count as zero bits. | Deployed feedback-policy benefit, generalization, benefit under corrected provisioning, or evidence for any catfish head. |
+| 5 | Multi-start `9.8698% / 3.5590%` | Shortfall **relative to best-found EE**, using hindsight numerator-specific selection among recorded endpoints and recorded F-best swaps. | A global ceiling, causal selector performance, a pure unilateral-search gain, or gains using the same denominator as `+17.03%`. |
+| 6 | `+113.412%`, `+133.58% / +119.12%`, and related control-law headlines | Capacity-based, realised-information control searches with fixed assignments; best-known feasible solutions, not certified optima. | Demand-capped achievable EE, a remaining opportunity after a causal baseline, or a C3 ceiling. |
+| 7 | Roughly `+0.7%–1.3%` coordination, old `+6.359%`, `+5.888%` interval | Particular bounded joint selectors compared with particular greedy endpoints, under particular rules, dates and reporting conventions. | The association layer's total physical headroom, a universal ranker ceiling, or a common interval for the present corrected comparison. |
+| 8 | Regret, ordering, R², collision, size, reachability and timing figures | Diagnostics of their named prediction problem, sample, implementation or instrument. | EE efficacy. None of the loss values is EE evidence. |
+
+**1. `FULLSPAN`: the headline is real for its experiment; your route attribution is not.** **V-code/V-receipt.** [FULLSPAN][fullspan] and [RESIDTOGGLE][toggle] specify the experiment. The [runner, lines 366–446][togglecode] evaluates candidates with `field="realised"`, all 48 boundaries, and constructs additive bits and energy as baseline plus the sum of complete-network singleton changes. There is no separate C2 forecast contribution in that construction. The catalogue includes association singletons, bundles, evacuations, adjacent-mode singletons, beam-wide controls, and joint association/control candidates.
+
+The declared C1 label instead contains a calibrated surplus and Phi; declared C2 consumes three offset projections. See [targets.py, lines 154–173][targets] and its `c2_persistence_forecast`. The pilot adds learned Q1 and Q2 differences in [its selector, lines 1524–1563][pilotselect]. Neither is the oracle singleton construction above. A 48-boundary immediate integral does not become the declared multi-step persistence target merely because both involve time.
+
+Your [07:45 state, lines 30–31][state] says “even if the residual is worth nothing, +10.80% stands.” It stands **as the outcome of that oracle additive selector on that catalogue**. It does not establish that C1+C2 are worth 10.80%, that their corpus supports those labels, or that their permitted actions include the controls producing the opportunity. This is convenient attribution without an identity connecting the objects.
+
+The oracle also filters candidates by **realised** served count before choosing them. The catalogue can be observable while the winning choice and its eligibility are clairvoyant. A causal implementation needs an information-compatible way to choose and guard actions; neither exact arithmetic nor a shared tape supplies that.
+
+**D.** The stage gains compose multiplicatively: `(1+0.108001)(1+0.056211)−1 ≈ 0.170283`. The residual stage contributes about **6.228 percentage points of baseline EE**, not 5.62 baseline points. Those are different denominators, not competing estimates.
+
+The **81.04% bits / 18.96% energy** division is an accounting path, not causal identification. The receipt first changes bits at old energy, then energy at new bits. Reversing the order gives approximately **16.66%** to energy; a logarithmic split gives approximately **17.79%**. The invariant facts are **+13.80% credited bits**, **−2.76% energy**, and **+17.03% EE**. The split does not identify physical mechanisms or route contributions.
+
+The aggregate service counts do not establish service non-inferiority. The report itself finds **39/800 user-anchor deliveries decrease**, with a worst decrease around 770 Mbit. `452→503` served means at least one decode somewhere in the horizon; `174→192` attained still leaves most user-anchors below target. Neither count measures uninterrupted service or protects individual users.
+
+“Whole-system span” here means the full selector contrast, not whole-spacecraft energy efficiency. The declared energy boundary is partial payload DC energy. Adding omitted policy-independent energy changes the percentage; in comparisons that trade fewer bits for lower energy it can even change the sign. FULLSPAN's simultaneous aggregate bit increase and energy decrease protects its sign under a common added energy term, but not its 17.03% magnitude or its transfer to another traffic numerator.
+
+**2. `RESIDTOGGLE`: a stronger comparator for total value than for component attribution.** **V-code.** [The optimizer, lines 511–565][toggleopt] uses actual numerator/energy for `WITH_RESIDUAL`, but `additive_numerator/additive_energy` for `ADDITIVE_ONLY`. It updates each arm's price from those respective quantities. Thus “one common price across eight anchors” does **not** mean one price shared between the arms. Enabling the residual also changes the converged price. This is a coherent comparison of two complete optimization procedures; it is not an intervention that holds the scoring price fixed and changes only one deployed head.
+
+**D.** A full exact optimizer can bound learned **total performance** on the identical finite product of catalogues, identical realised admissibility set and identical reporting objective. The zero Dinkelbach residual supplies the certificate: at its price every eligible combination has `N−eta*E≤0`, with equality for the selected combination, so none has a higher ratio when energy is positive. This is a finite hindsight bound, not a global assignment/control bound.
+
+That theorem does **not** bound a learned **marginal** by an oracle marginal. For example, let three equal-energy candidates have true values `(10,9,0)`, exact additive parts `(8,9,0)` and residuals `(2,0,0)`. Exact residual removal changes value from 10 to 9: marginal 1. With learned additive estimates `(0.9,0,1)`, the same exact residual changes the selected value from 0 to 10: marginal 10. The full value respects the oracle ceiling; the component marginal exceeds the oracle marginal tenfold. No physics change is needed.
+
+Likewise, an erroneous prediction can preserve every ranking, so “strictly less whenever the head errs” is false. And exact optimization of a selection proxy need not maximize reported EE at all. The gate needs these qualifications before it is used to terminate or fund a design.
+
+**3. The sign contradiction is an unmatched comparison with two omitted confounders.** **V-code/V-receipt.** [C3REACH's measurement, lines 260–286][reachcode] computes learned Q1+Q2 differences, then adds exact Ψ. It never replaces the additive terms by their exact counterparts. `RESIDTOGGLE` does. Your four proposed explanations omit that distinction even though your earlier parametrisation record explains why hybrid exact/learned scores can fail badly.
+
+There is a second omitted distinction. [EVALPATH, lines 102–107][evalpath] documents that the primitive builder scalar-caches a full-trajectory base, while pilot exact-interaction calculations can combine it with dense boundary-0 candidates. C3REACH reuses precisely that builder's evaluator at [lines 216–242][reachstart]. “Exact Ψ” therefore means exactly computed from those supplied profiles, not authenticated as the declared same-horizon residual.
+
+**D.** This error can scale with coalition size. If the joint and its `k` singletons use the snapshot but the reference uses the trajectory, define `delta = G(base,trajectory) − G(base,snapshot)`. Then `Psi_mixed = Psi_snapshot + (k−1)*delta`. A baseline discrepancy becomes a 99-fold residual discrepancy at a hundred-user coalition. Thus a very large “exact Ψ” can itself be an evaluator artefact; comparing learned and exact score ranges cannot diagnose model scaling until that identity is reconciled.
+
+The approximately −60% magnitude is conditional on **48 changed decisions**, not all 80. Retain that denominator. In this receipt the with-residual pool has both fewer bits and more joules; adding identical unchanged decisions preserves the negative sign, but need not preserve the percentage. Carrier variants and learner seeds also do not turn seven physical steps on one world into 80 independent physical replications.
+
+The accurate joint statement is: **the hindsight full-surplus optimizer improves on its additive surrogate; inserting the pilot's exact-residual calculation into its learned additive scores is harmful on the changed-decision subset.** Both may be true. Price-only or gate-only findings cannot automatically reconcile them.
+
+**4. Mode selection is the strongest demonstrated causal-information candidate, with a narrower meaning of “causal.”** **V-code/V-receipt.** [MODE-CAUSAL][mode] really does report demand-capped `3.892083→6.928825 Mbit/J`, fixed energy, and zero credit on failed decoding. Its code uses a previous-boundary history before updating that history: [lines 209–286][modecode]. I found no current-SINR selection in R2/R3; that is reserved for R4.
+
+But history contains **exact simulated SINR for every powered record**, including records without a successful data decode. It assumes feedback for the same user/beam at the preceding TDM phase, with no estimation error, feedback energy, signalling cost or additional delay represented in this comparison. Whether the intended system can obtain and deliver that CQI is **UNDETERMINED**; an observation and latency contract would settle it. The rule is non-anticipating in this simulator, not operationally validated.
+
+The `25.79%→13.46%` failure comparison is **R2 versus R3**, not either against R0, whose all-record failure share is **0.84%** and no-mode share **78.49%**. Conditional on selecting a mode, R2/R3 fail **44.34% / 28.71%**. Those rates are already charged in the EE result, so they do not invalidate it. They do invalidate a casual claim that the policy improves reliability over the declared rule. Report no-mode, success and failure together, plus user-level service.
+
+The `+111.72%` best R1 sensitivity point is outcome-selected within its sweep, not a deployable rule chosen prospectively. R4's `+248.86%` capped gain is a current-realised-SINR oracle. Neither can be substituted for the pre-specified stale-CQI comparison. The `+78%` was measured under the nominal-power convention; it cannot be transferred to corrected provisioning or added to an assignment gain measured elsewhere.
+
+**5. Assignment search: existence of better recorded assignments, not a ceiling.** **V-receipt.** [MULTISTART-DEMAND-CAPPED][multistart] gives both denominator conventions explicitly:
+
+| Rule | Reference EE | Best-found EE | Gain over reference | Reference shortfall from best |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| SEALED | 34.570961 | 38.356680 | **10.9506%** | 9.8698% |
+| MARGIN_Q | 43.633671 | 45.243918 | **3.6904%** | 3.5590% |
+
+All EEs are Mbit/J. The reference is the **nearest-start search endpoint**, not the raw nearest-eligible incumbent used by FULLSPAN. Best-found includes recorded swaps, so it is not purely a benefit of changing unilateral start. Selection among records uses their realised reporting-numerator EE; a causal start-selection rule has not been demonstrated. Best-per-anchor selection followed by pooling is also not generally the pooled optimum.
+
+The 768 replay fields, nine 1-ULP differences, exact served counts and matching identities authenticate the rescore. They do not certify optimality or generalization. The receipt supports all 128 endpoints being non-optimal for two-swaps under the selection score, but only **2/2 predeclared endpoints** were fully checked under capped committed EE: best gains **1.7177% / 0.8182%**. Do not promote 2/2 to 128/128 or two-swap failure to single-user failure.
+
+**6. Control-law and historical numbers.** **V-receipt.** [FAST LOOK][fastlook] uses realised modes and capacity; [CONTROL-LAW-CEILING][control] explicitly says its `+133.58% / +119.12%` values are best-known, not certified. The local probe's approximately 97.9% recovery does not bound a per-user residual: one beam's rule can already coordinate all users sharing that beam. Its per-beam local choices also need joint execution with recomputed interference before being treated as a feasible combined controller.
+
+Your supplied `+113.412%→+0.273%` correction is **not independently verified here**. The [capped fast-look report I opened][fastcap] says the capped value was not recoverable from its written receipts. It also describes **capping per-boundary rate before integration**, whereas FULLSPAN, MULTISTART and MODE-CAUSAL cap **integrated per-user delivery**. Those are different traffic metrics. The provenance and exact cap placement behind `+0.273%` are **UNDETERMINED**; the selected per-user delivery ledger and the later rescore would settle them. I am not rejecting your supplied correction, but I will not repeat it as a receipt I verified.
+
+**D.** In general, `integral min(rate,demand) ≤ min(integral rate, demand×duration)`. The right side allows surplus at one time to compensate deficit at another. Neither establishes queueing delay or continuous service. This is a plausible next numerator overturning even after everyone agrees to say “demand-capped.”
+
+The old spans and intervals remain descriptive evidence for their exact configurations. The thirty-date `+0.717% [0.436,0.997]` uses old pairing; the corrected twenty-anchor `+1.2913%` has **6/20**, not the **1/20** negatives printed in [STATUS, line 23][status]. The latest width comparison gives `+0.899421%`, **1/8** negative. You cannot attach one panel's interval to another panel's point estimate or transfer its variance unchanged after a policy change. The earlier `+5.888% [5.235,6.540]` interval belongs to the earlier provisioning condition.
+
+Your several-hundred-percent prefix gains are gains of the nonlearned search over geometry. They cannot become learned gains because a head is placed downstream. Conversely, the small increment of one bounded joint catalogue cannot cap all association improvement. “Mispaired” was too strong for an honestly paired joint extension of its own seed: that experiment estimates a valid conditional extension. Its defect was treating one traversal's endpoint as a canonical comparator.
+
+**7. The remaining quantitative evidence needs the following limits.** The table audits what the controller records claim. Where no opened worker/source evidence is cited above, the empirical value remains record-level evidence; the restrictions on what follows from it are deductions, not independent replications.
