codex
**Your training gate treats oracle contrasts from a different decision problem as upper bounds on the contribution of the declared three learned routes.**

This is an audit of your reasoning. I read the 90 controller records and traced the consequential claims into the worker reports and source identified below. I ran no measurements, fits, optimization searches or simulations. I used one `nice -n 15 /usr/bin/python3` process for arithmetic on printed numbers. I did not access `/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover` or its virtual environment. This report is the only file I created or changed.

Evidence labels: **V-code** means source I opened; **V-receipt** means a worker receipt/report I opened, not an independently repeated experiment; **D** means a derivation; **I** means an inference. A controller record proves that you asserted something, not that it happened. I kept `OBJMISMATCH`, `C1REAL`, `EXACTGEN`, `SIGNFORK` and `FACTORIAL` outputs unopened, including any report file that appeared during this audit. Their reading rules below therefore do not depend on their results.

The error in the first sentence has two independently checkable parts. Your [training gate, lines 14–17][gate] says an exact route marginal is an upper bound on a learned marginal, “strictly less whenever the head errs.” That is false in general. And `FULLSPAN`'s additive scorer is not the declared C1/C2 pair: it sums exact realised singleton changes over association **and power/mode controls**, then solves its own pooled surrogate ratio. Its full scorer optimizes realised outcomes with hindsight. Calling these “exact terms” does not make them exact implementations of your three heads.

You have already recorded the evidence against your gate: [PARAMETRISATION][param] reports that replacing either learned half by its exact counterpart worsens selection regret, from 3.618 to 9.043 or 9.647. This is evidence about ranking, not EE. It is nevertheless directly contrary to the monotonic “more exact component means better decision” premise you subsequently installed as a compute gate. Your own stages 6–8 contract amendment v1.2, item 3, also explicitly allows a learned selector to improve realised EE under model mismatch while remaining bounded by the exact selector on their common selection score.

**Q1 — The evidence ledger, ranked by damage.**

The arithmetic is usually the least troublesome part. The main failure is carrying a number across a change in decision object, information, reference, target, or population without carrying that change with it.

| Rank | Number you are carrying | What it actually measures | What it cannot establish |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `FULLSPAN +17.03%`; additive `+10.80%` | Eight-anchor, corrected-provisioning, hindsight catalogue comparison against an unsearched nearest-eligible incumbent. Full EE is 9.029226 versus 7.715422 Mbit/J. Additive is 8.548697. | Benefit, learnability, necessity, or attainable gain of the declared three learned heads; benefit over a competent search baseline. |
| 2 | `RESIDTOGGLE +5.62%` | Full exact pooled-EE optimization versus a singleton-additive surrogate optimizer, with a separate optimized price for each arm. Same expanded catalogue and realised service filter. | The maximum possible C3 source-training effect; a clean fixed-price residual toggle in the deployed pilot. |
| 3 | `C3REACH 30.82 → 12.30 Mbit/J`, approximately `−60.09%` | Adding an “exact” residual to **learned** additive scores, pooled over the 48 changed anchor-seed decisions. The upstream pilot evaluator has a documented mixed-boundary problem. | A negative full-exact-system result directly contradicting `FULLSPAN`, or proof that interaction itself hurts EE. |
| 4 | Causal mode selection `+78.02%`, `+76.64%` | Fixed-power re-crediting on one world, four anchors, using exact one-boundary-old simulated SINR; failures count as zero bits. | Deployed feedback-policy benefit, generalization, benefit under corrected provisioning, or evidence for any catfish head. |
| 5 | Multi-start `9.8698% / 3.5590%` | Shortfall **relative to best-found EE**, using hindsight numerator-specific selection among recorded endpoints and recorded F-best swaps. | A global ceiling, causal selector performance, a pure unilateral-search gain, or gains using the same denominator as `+17.03%`. |
| 6 | `+113.412%`, `+133.58% / +119.12%`, and related control-law headlines | Capacity-based, realised-information control searches with fixed assignments; best-known feasible solutions, not certified optima. | Demand-capped achievable EE, a remaining opportunity after a causal baseline, or a C3 ceiling. |
| 7 | Roughly `+0.7%–1.3%` coordination, old `+6.359%`, `+5.888%` interval | Particular bounded joint selectors compared with particular greedy endpoints, under particular rules, dates and reporting conventions. | The association layer's total physical headroom, a universal ranker ceiling, or a common interval for the present corrected comparison. |
| 8 | Regret, ordering, R², collision, size, reachability and timing figures | Diagnostics of their named prediction problem, sample, implementation or instrument. | EE efficacy. None of the loss values is EE evidence. |

**1. `FULLSPAN`: the headline is real for its experiment; your route attribution is not.** **V-code/V-receipt.** [FULLSPAN][fullspan] and [RESIDTOGGLE][toggle] specify the experiment. The [runner, lines 366–446][togglecode] evaluates candidates with `field="realised"`, all 48 boundaries, and constructs additive bits and energy as baseline plus the sum of complete-network singleton changes. There is no separate C2 forecast contribution in that construction. The catalogue includes association singletons, bundles, evacuations, adjacent-mode singletons, beam-wide controls, and joint association/control candidates.

The declared C1 label instead contains a calibrated surplus and Phi; declared C2 consumes three offset projections. See [targets.py, lines 154–173][targets] and its `c2_persistence_forecast`. The pilot adds learned Q1 and Q2 differences in [its selector, lines 1524–1563][pilotselect]. Neither is the oracle singleton construction above. A 48-boundary immediate integral does not become the declared multi-step persistence target merely because both involve time.

Your [07:45 state, lines 30–31][state] says “even if the residual is worth nothing, +10.80% stands.” It stands **as the outcome of that oracle additive selector on that catalogue**. It does not establish that C1+C2 are worth 10.80%, that their corpus supports those labels, or that their permitted actions include the controls producing the opportunity. This is convenient attribution without an identity connecting the objects.

The oracle also filters candidates by **realised** served count before choosing them. The catalogue can be observable while the winning choice and its eligibility are clairvoyant. A causal implementation needs an information-compatible way to choose and guard actions; neither exact arithmetic nor a shared tape supplies that.

**D.** The stage gains compose multiplicatively: `(1+0.108001)(1+0.056211)−1 ≈ 0.170283`. The residual stage contributes about **6.228 percentage points of baseline EE**, not 5.62 baseline points. Those are different denominators, not competing estimates.

The **81.04% bits / 18.96% energy** division is an accounting path, not causal identification. The receipt first changes bits at old energy, then energy at new bits. Reversing the order gives approximately **16.66%** to energy; a logarithmic split gives approximately **17.79%**. The invariant facts are **+13.80% credited bits**, **−2.76% energy**, and **+17.03% EE**. The split does not identify physical mechanisms or route contributions.

The aggregate service counts do not establish service non-inferiority. The report itself finds **39/800 user-anchor deliveries decrease**, with a worst decrease around 770 Mbit. `452→503` served means at least one decode somewhere in the horizon; `174→192` attained still leaves most user-anchors below target. Neither count measures uninterrupted service or protects individual users.

“Whole-system span” here means the full selector contrast, not whole-spacecraft energy efficiency. The declared energy boundary is partial payload DC energy. Adding omitted policy-independent energy changes the percentage; in comparisons that trade fewer bits for lower energy it can even change the sign. FULLSPAN's simultaneous aggregate bit increase and energy decrease protects its sign under a common added energy term, but not its 17.03% magnitude or its transfer to another traffic numerator.

**2. `RESIDTOGGLE`: a stronger comparator for total value than for component attribution.** **V-code.** [The optimizer, lines 511–565][toggleopt] uses actual numerator/energy for `WITH_RESIDUAL`, but `additive_numerator/additive_energy` for `ADDITIVE_ONLY`. It updates each arm's price from those respective quantities. Thus “one common price across eight anchors” does **not** mean one price shared between the arms. Enabling the residual also changes the converged price. This is a coherent comparison of two complete optimization procedures; it is not an intervention that holds the scoring price fixed and changes only one deployed head.

**D.** A full exact optimizer can bound learned **total performance** on the identical finite product of catalogues, identical realised admissibility set and identical reporting objective. The zero Dinkelbach residual supplies the certificate: at its price every eligible combination has `N−eta*E≤0`, with equality for the selected combination, so none has a higher ratio when energy is positive. This is a finite hindsight bound, not a global assignment/control bound.

That theorem does **not** bound a learned **marginal** by an oracle marginal. For example, let three equal-energy candidates have true values `(10,9,0)`, exact additive parts `(8,9,0)` and residuals `(2,0,0)`. Exact residual removal changes value from 10 to 9: marginal 1. With learned additive estimates `(0.9,0,1)`, the same exact residual changes the selected value from 0 to 10: marginal 10. The full value respects the oracle ceiling; the component marginal exceeds the oracle marginal tenfold. No physics change is needed.

Likewise, an erroneous prediction can preserve every ranking, so “strictly less whenever the head errs” is false. And exact optimization of a selection proxy need not maximize reported EE at all. The gate needs these qualifications before it is used to terminate or fund a design.

**3. The sign contradiction is an unmatched comparison with two omitted confounders.** **V-code/V-receipt.** [C3REACH's measurement, lines 260–286][reachcode] computes learned Q1+Q2 differences, then adds exact Ψ. It never replaces the additive terms by their exact counterparts. `RESIDTOGGLE` does. Your four proposed explanations omit that distinction even though your earlier parametrisation record explains why hybrid exact/learned scores can fail badly.

There is a second omitted distinction. [EVALPATH, lines 102–107][evalpath] documents that the primitive builder scalar-caches a full-trajectory base, while pilot exact-interaction calculations can combine it with dense boundary-0 candidates. C3REACH reuses precisely that builder's evaluator at [lines 216–242][reachstart]. “Exact Ψ” therefore means exactly computed from those supplied profiles, not authenticated as the declared same-horizon residual.

**D.** This error can scale with coalition size. If the joint and its `k` singletons use the snapshot but the reference uses the trajectory, define `delta = G(base,trajectory) − G(base,snapshot)`. Then `Psi_mixed = Psi_snapshot + (k−1)*delta`. A baseline discrepancy becomes a 99-fold residual discrepancy at a hundred-user coalition. Thus a very large “exact Ψ” can itself be an evaluator artefact; comparing learned and exact score ranges cannot diagnose model scaling until that identity is reconciled.

The approximately −60% magnitude is conditional on **48 changed decisions**, not all 80. Retain that denominator. In this receipt the with-residual pool has both fewer bits and more joules; adding identical unchanged decisions preserves the negative sign, but need not preserve the percentage. Carrier variants and learner seeds also do not turn seven physical steps on one world into 80 independent physical replications.

The accurate joint statement is: **the hindsight full-surplus optimizer improves on its additive surrogate; inserting the pilot's exact-residual calculation into its learned additive scores is harmful on the changed-decision subset.** Both may be true. Price-only or gate-only findings cannot automatically reconcile them.

**4. Mode selection is the strongest demonstrated causal-information candidate, with a narrower meaning of “causal.”** **V-code/V-receipt.** [MODE-CAUSAL][mode] really does report demand-capped `3.892083→6.928825 Mbit/J`, fixed energy, and zero credit on failed decoding. Its code uses a previous-boundary history before updating that history: [lines 209–286][modecode]. I found no current-SINR selection in R2/R3; that is reserved for R4.

But history contains **exact simulated SINR for every powered record**, including records without a successful data decode. It assumes feedback for the same user/beam at the preceding TDM phase, with no estimation error, feedback energy, signalling cost or additional delay represented in this comparison. Whether the intended system can obtain and deliver that CQI is **UNDETERMINED**; an observation and latency contract would settle it. The rule is non-anticipating in this simulator, not operationally validated.

The `25.79%→13.46%` failure comparison is **R2 versus R3**, not either against R0, whose all-record failure share is **0.84%** and no-mode share **78.49%**. Conditional on selecting a mode, R2/R3 fail **44.34% / 28.71%**. Those rates are already charged in the EE result, so they do not invalidate it. They do invalidate a casual claim that the policy improves reliability over the declared rule. Report no-mode, success and failure together, plus user-level service.

The `+111.72%` best R1 sensitivity point is outcome-selected within its sweep, not a deployable rule chosen prospectively. R4's `+248.86%` capped gain is a current-realised-SINR oracle. Neither can be substituted for the pre-specified stale-CQI comparison. The `+78%` was measured under the nominal-power convention; it cannot be transferred to corrected provisioning or added to an assignment gain measured elsewhere.

**5. Assignment search: existence of better recorded assignments, not a ceiling.** **V-receipt.** [MULTISTART-DEMAND-CAPPED][multistart] gives both denominator conventions explicitly:

| Rule | Reference EE | Best-found EE | Gain over reference | Reference shortfall from best |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| SEALED | 34.570961 | 38.356680 | **10.9506%** | 9.8698% |
| MARGIN_Q | 43.633671 | 45.243918 | **3.6904%** | 3.5590% |

All EEs are Mbit/J. The reference is the **nearest-start search endpoint**, not the raw nearest-eligible incumbent used by FULLSPAN. Best-found includes recorded swaps, so it is not purely a benefit of changing unilateral start. Selection among records uses their realised reporting-numerator EE; a causal start-selection rule has not been demonstrated. Best-per-anchor selection followed by pooling is also not generally the pooled optimum.

The 768 replay fields, nine 1-ULP differences, exact served counts and matching identities authenticate the rescore. They do not certify optimality or generalization. The receipt supports all 128 endpoints being non-optimal for two-swaps under the selection score, but only **2/2 predeclared endpoints** were fully checked under capped committed EE: best gains **1.7177% / 0.8182%**. Do not promote 2/2 to 128/128 or two-swap failure to single-user failure.

**6. Control-law and historical numbers.** **V-receipt.** [FAST LOOK][fastlook] uses realised modes and capacity; [CONTROL-LAW-CEILING][control] explicitly says its `+133.58% / +119.12%` values are best-known, not certified. The local probe's approximately 97.9% recovery does not bound a per-user residual: one beam's rule can already coordinate all users sharing that beam. Its per-beam local choices also need joint execution with recomputed interference before being treated as a feasible combined controller.

Your supplied `+113.412%→+0.273%` correction is **not independently verified here**. The [capped fast-look report I opened][fastcap] says the capped value was not recoverable from its written receipts. It also describes **capping per-boundary rate before integration**, whereas FULLSPAN, MULTISTART and MODE-CAUSAL cap **integrated per-user delivery**. Those are different traffic metrics. The provenance and exact cap placement behind `+0.273%` are **UNDETERMINED**; the selected per-user delivery ledger and the later rescore would settle them. I am not rejecting your supplied correction, but I will not repeat it as a receipt I verified.

**D.** In general, `integral min(rate,demand) ≤ min(integral rate, demand×duration)`. The right side allows surplus at one time to compensate deficit at another. Neither establishes queueing delay or continuous service. This is a plausible next numerator overturning even after everyone agrees to say “demand-capped.”

The old spans and intervals remain descriptive evidence for their exact configurations. The thirty-date `+0.717% [0.436,0.997]` uses old pairing; the corrected twenty-anchor `+1.2913%` has **6/20**, not the **1/20** negatives printed in [STATUS, line 23][status]. The latest width comparison gives `+0.899421%`, **1/8** negative. You cannot attach one panel's interval to another panel's point estimate or transfer its variance unchanged after a policy change. The earlier `+5.888% [5.235,6.540]` interval belongs to the earlier provisioning condition.

Your several-hundred-percent prefix gains are gains of the nonlearned search over geometry. They cannot become learned gains because a head is placed downstream. Conversely, the small increment of one bounded joint catalogue cannot cap all association improvement. “Mispaired” was too strong for an honestly paired joint extension of its own seed: that experiment estimates a valid conditional extension. Its defect was treating one traversal's endpoint as a canonical comparator.

**7. The remaining quantitative evidence needs the following limits.** The table audits what the controller records claim. Where no opened worker/source evidence is cited above, the empirical value remains record-level evidence; the restrictions on what follows from it are deductions, not independent replications.

| Metric family in the records | Admissible reading | Overreach still at risk |
|---|---|---|
| 27.8% pairwise winner reversals; 92% above a margin; shortlist recovery | Exact pair calibration fails to reproduce the chosen exact-score winners in those labelled pools. | Calling the score gap a +0.5% reported-EE effect, or proving every refitted pairwise ranker inadequate. |
| Regret 3.618 vs size prior 13.114 vs zero 13.683; direct 2.427 | Those particular estimators rank those pools differently under `ΔF/κ`. | “C3 is worth 9.496” in EE, size is generally useless, or direct prediction is a proven deployment improvement. The parametrisation corpus lacks per-row served-count receipts. |
| 22.99 parts-to-total ratio; error correlation −0.788; amplification 0.887 | Worst-case relative sensitivity versus observed error cancellation on a particular fit. | Independence is **not** an assumption of the worst-case bound; good error correlation does not remove conditioning or guarantee it survives migration. |
| C1 R² 0.151/order 0.650; oracle order 0.902; surrogate 0.598/0.801 | Different targets and different available information. The 0.151 result is the production-shaped `16→8→1` MLP, not the “linear model” your corpus finding calls it. | An information-theoretic ceiling or achievable 0.902 after a cheap feature repair. The oracle still knows coupled energy. |
| 79.3% coupled contribution; 98.9% within-anchor variation | The former is a **covariance allocation** to externality plus energy; the latter rules out a purely anchor-constant externality. | “79.3% is unpredictable,” “only 2.1% is available before decision,” or “none cancels.” Cost to calculate a label does not prove inability to predict it. |
| 176,223 rows; rank 14; effective 12 scalar degrees; 1e6 sentinel; 822/1,784 bad survival rows | Corpus/schema and adapter diagnostics on the audited populations. | Effective sample size, exact-target coverage, current-corpus rates after regeneration, or proof that all previous exact-target diagnostics used surrogates. Your corpus record itself cites an exact-target diagnostic. |
| 14/20 or 20/20 anchors with a flip; 79.164% context-less rows; large score ranges | Reachability and score-scale diagnostics. Actual flip counts are 48/80 exact and 75/80 learned. | A useful contribution, independent replications, or a 20.8% ceiling on how often C3 can alter the winner. |
| 30/30 mechanism witnesses, 28/30 activation, 29/30 evacuation, 0/30 relief | Presence/absence within the searched families and operating condition. | Population prevalence, necessity of learning, or proof the unobserved mechanism cannot occur. Three occupants are **not** three movers: two arrivals can activate occupancy three. |
| 94.8% PA share; +53% after changing provisioning | Accounting share and a comparison under different policies. | PA share of whole-spacecraft energy, association irrelevance, or +53% available for a new algorithm. Association changes occupancy, interference, power and activation. |
| 81.74%/87.85% anytime recovery; 65 s; 49.03 s vs 632.83 s; 29.42 h; checkpoint round trips | Particular timing/cost or serialization evidence, with their workloads and exclusions. | Proof no learned anytime advantage exists, full-panel affordability, route validity, or an EE success probability. |
| 30 dates, 160 planned dates, 166 usable files; assumed SDs; 3–5 or 16 seeds; “3–3.5 in 10” | Inventory, design assumptions, simulations or personal judgement as labelled. | Independent date generalization by counting seeds/anchors, demonstrated power for a revised claim, or a calibrated probability of project success. |

**Q2 — Load-bearing premises that remain wrong or unverified.**

**A. “The exact path repairs the data while preserving the inputs needed by a cheap predictor.” Wrong. V-code/V-receipt.** The [exact builder, lines 599–672][exactinputs] fills Q1 features from the candidate's evaluated margin, required power and ACM efficiency; Q2 features include evaluated future projections. [The cost receipt][rowcost] identifies those suppliers explicitly. The [data census][census] finds all Q1 and Q2 state vectors differ across the two paths at both diffed anchors. Switching paths changes features as well as labels, despite retaining the same dimensional schema. Some feature acquisition requires the very candidate solve the head is supposed to avoid. That may be allowed in an offline teacher; it is not free inference. The deployment feature supplier and its cost remain **UNDETERMINED** for the proposed successor.

**B. “Failure of a high-capacity model proves an informational ceiling.” Wrong. D.** The training gate G2 and [bakeoff metric 3][bakeoff] assert this. Finite-sample failure can arise from estimation, optimization, regularization, distribution shift, scaling or the tested model family. A collision witness can prove non-identifiability for those states; a validated distributional lower bound can quantify its prevalence. A failed fit cannot. Success would establish useful predictability on that held-out support, not a universal architectural diagnosis. The gate turns an inconclusive result into an impossibility proof and can stop useful work for the wrong reason.

**C. “Missing contexts restrict C3 to changing about one fifth of catalogues/decisions.” Wrong as a frequency bound. V-code/D.** [Pilot lines 1509–1515][pilotcontexts] create contexts for every legal row with at least two changed users. The missing rows are the empty/singleton case under that rule. Their mutual scores cannot change, but **one** altered multi-user row can overtake every singleton at every anchor. A 79% row share gives no 21% bound on decision reachability. C3REACH's exact branch applies exact Ψ to **all** legal rows; the context gate is explicitly on the learned branch. A gate fork on an exact residual that is correctly zero for empty/singleton sets should be a no-op unless the factor changes something else.

**D. “The residual sign is primarily a price-versus-context question.” Incomplete. V-code.** Learned versus exact additive background and mixed-horizon residual construction are missing from the declared causal story. The open-contradiction record also says a price explanation would be repairable “without touching any of the three routes.” That does not follow: C1 and Ψ are price-dependent targets. Changing eta changes labels, scale and potentially training, even if the architecture stays fixed.

**E. “There is one head-independent certified fixed point, hence a universal floor and degeneracy test.” Conditional, then overextended. D/V-record.** A deterministic algorithm with fixed initial state, ordering, objective and guard has one reproducible output. Head independence alone does not specify those ingredients, and your arm-owned-seed design changes an ingredient. The certified reference can be common only by an explicit separate construction. More seriously, [the degeneracy screen][degeneracy] conditions on **every compared arm's observed performance** exceeding the reference. Its restricted estimate describes a selected successful subset, not an unbiased source effect. Printing the all-anchor result beside it makes the selection visible; it does not make it causal. A neutral arm's worse performance can be a real source-training effect while still failing to justify the whole architecture against a strong baseline.

**F. “A trained full/drop comparison, an exact-term knockout and a physical interaction are interchangeable.” Wrong. V-record/D.** Your erratum 14 separates these; the training gate merges them again. A fixed-model output knockout, a retrained neutral-source substitution, and a different exact optimizer are three interventions. The physical identity `Ψ(A)=ΔF(A)−Σd_i` is not the statistical interaction of the eight training-source cells. Likewise, single-route benefit versus all-neutral is not single-route benefit versus raw geometry.

**G. “The certified unilateral endpoint is a Nash equilibrium and the bounded gap is price of anarchy.” Unsupported as stated.** [TERMINOLOGY][terminology] supplies neither a game with players' payoffs and feasible deviations nor a worst-equilibrium/global-social-optimum comparison. The code searches a common guarded network objective. One could define an identical-interest constrained game around it, but that is an additional modelling statement. A bounded candidate maximum versus one endpoint is not a price-of-anarchy estimate. The accompanying “few per cent is typical” does not establish this system's limit. Use “this search's local endpoint and its bounded joint extension.”

**H. “Energy is set by the control law, not association; interaction is stronger at the power object; mode control is orthogonal to the decomposition.” Unsupported. D.** A law maps state and assignment into powers. Fixing the law does not fix energy across assignments. Nor does a stronger coupling coefficient prove greater decision value for a residual head. Mode changes alter credited bits, the usefulness of assignments and their interactions, so they are not quantitatively orthogonal interventions. The strategic-energy record and bakeoff silently assume this transfer.

**I. “The exact corpus costs 49.03 seconds per anchor; the discrepant 632.83 seconds used different row densities.” First is partial; second is contradicted by the receipts. V-receipt.** Both reports measured **992 rows**. The 49.03-second benchmark excluded coalition construction, full legal-action enumeration, tape setup, training and endpoints; its two anchors are two carriers of the **same physical step**. The 632.83-second report also says 992 rows. Different execution work or configuration may explain the difference, but row density has not. `AFFORDABLE` applies to the scoped source-row component, not the training programme. EXACTGEN must reconcile actual work counters and settings before either rate is extrapolated.

**J. “Predeclared means statistically unselected; unchanged numbers mean the estimand is unchanged.” Wrong. V-record/D.** The [requirement change][requirement] openly occurred after +5.62% was seen. The owner is entitled to change the goal. That creates an exploratory new claim and changes what success means, even if no number is recomputed. “Substantial” has no numerical decision rule, so G1 is not a determinate pass/fail test yet. Similarly, keeping the existing beam width because it was the “most stable point sampled” is an outcome-based justification for retention. Keeping a previously fixed value is defensible; claiming the exposure to favourable-antenna selection “disappears entirely” is not. Do not repair this by picking a fresh threshold from the same results.

**K. “Two independent reviewers establish the premise.” Wrong.** Reviewer independence is not evidence independence when both consume your same false selector statement or the same receipt. The state says every surviving finding has two sources; the calibration history demonstrates that this is insufficient. For execution claims, identify the executed entry point and imported source, then connect it to the receipt. I checked SHA-256 for the pilot selector, residual-toggle runner and mode-causal script; all three match the hashes printed in their reports. That authenticates the inspected files, not every assertion made about them.

Other categorical claims should be demoted, without commissioning another broad measurement campaign:

- Small correlation with satellite count does not prove the date variation is “not constellation growth”; a single-month panel does not isolate geometry completely. Near-zero rank correlation does not make every prediction using the old rule worthless.
- The failed load sweep closes that sampled hypothesis, not every coordination direction. An anytime comparator recovering 82–88% of its own gain does not prove no faster learned method could improve the remaining portion.
- “All earlier learnability evidence used surrogates” contradicts the exact-target 0.151 diagnostic cited in the same corpus finding. Preserve separate provenance, rather than invalidating everything wholesale.
- A two-arrival occupancy-three witness is a pair interaction. The records repeatedly turn final occupancy three into a requirement for three changed users. Higher-order evidence must come from its own mixed differences/reversals.
- A 32-pair block plus a summed omitted-pair residual preserves aggregate magnitude, not the identities of all omitted aggressors. “Nothing lost silently” must not become “full pairwise structure retained.”
- “2 ULP is fixed by IEEE 754” is false. Floating-point format determines ULP spacing, not this algorithm's allowable accumulated error. A 2-ULP gate is a declared engineering tolerance; a 1-ULP discrepancy alone does not prove summation order. Preserve exact identity checks and reason about reduction error separately.
- The screen's rules “validation still falling means undertrained” and “oscillating means learning rate too high” are diagnoses stated as certainties. Neither curve shape uniquely identifies its cause; neither bears directly on EE.
- The claim that the mechanism paper is closed on novelty is **UNDETERMINED** here. I did not independently audit the cited literature. The records' twelve-paper inventory cannot settle all publishable questions, and their own assertions about full-buffer versus demand-limited conventions conflict. A claim-by-claim primary-source comparison would settle novelty; reviewer preference cannot.
- Your score/Phi adjudication left `network_objective` unresolved. I opened [its body, lines 130–144][objective]: it returns `bits − eta*joules`, without Phi. That narrow open question is settled by code; it does not authenticate every caller's composite score.

**Q3 — The three-route structure is not established as the right scientific object.**

**I.** The measured EE story is presently dominated by **search and control-policy choices whose gains have not been attributed to the three catfish sources**. That is the honest answer to the owner's concern. It is not a proof that the physics prohibits three useful heads. The available measurements simply do not select this decomposition over alternatives.

Even the premise “headroom sits outside the heads” needs qualification. Assignment search is a plausible consumer of learned guidance, and temporal CQI makes persistence potentially useful. Those are hypotheses about a new consumer or observation model, not evidence that the present targets and deployment have the right interfaces. The `9.87%` and `+78%` cannot rank research directions quantitatively: they use different reference quality, provisioning, information and candidate restrictions. FULLSPAN itself crosses the association/control boundary you are using to separate those directions.

Your newer requirement removes the argument used to close direct prediction: preserving three individually positive routes is no longer the scientific test. The owner still wants a three-route design, but that is an architectural preference until the contributions or practical advantages are demonstrated. Three numbers that sum exactly are an accounting decomposition; they are not automatically three separately learnable sources or three necessary modules.

The bakeoff's proposed information partition has another unresolved dependency: conditional expectations `E[Y|I]` are population objects, not exact per-row quantities supplied by the physics evaluator. Evaluating that candidate requires a distribution and an estimation procedure. “Offline, with no training” cannot by itself deliver the stipulated held-out model comparisons. Target correlation also does not prove independent information sources, and low correlation does not guarantee useful separate decisions.

The paper can presently support a **model-conditional diagnostic account**: which objective, information and control conventions create the apparent association opportunity; how much finite catalogue hindsight improvement exists; and where a declared causal feedback rule improves same-power credited delivery on the measured tape. Novelty and external validity remain to be established. It cannot currently claim three successful catfish routes or operational energy savings.

A subsequent positive paper could claim **a specified causal controller reaches a stated fraction of a bounded reference's quality at a measured end-to-end cost**, with service distributions and out-of-development evaluation; or **informative source training improves a named controller over its neutral-source version**. Those are different claims and can coexist. Neither requires pretending the exact factorial is a learned-source experiment. A cheap deterministic control rule can be a valuable result if it explains and removes the dominant waste; the number of neural heads is not the contribution by itself.

The fastest defensible route to training is to stop making the measurements decide questions they do not identify. Fix one written mapping from intended observation → features → targets → candidate actions → score → guard → reported endpoint, using the already available code and receipts. Name the new current claim and its reference. Then a bounded learned pilot can answer a learned question. Do not wait for a finite fit to prove an informational theorem, and do not use a positive oracle factorial as proof that the mapping already exists.

**Q4 — Ranked predictions of the next overturning, with checks below one hour.**

These are proposed checks, not runs I performed. Each uses already declared contrasts or audits the existing evidence; none selects a rerun by a favourable outcome. Times are human-work estimates for bounded inspection/arithmetic, not measured runtime promises.

| Rank | Claim most likely to fall next | Mechanism | Cheapest concrete check |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | “FACTORIAL measures the exact contributions of our C1/C2/C3.” | FULLSPAN has one exact singleton term and a residual, with different controls, horizon, guard and price from the heads. A third factor can be invented merely by naming an algebraic split C2. | **20–40 min, no physics:** write each factorial factor as a formula and identify its target function, offset set, units and selector use. Require the full cell to reconstruct the intended score and distinguish `000` from external BASELINE. If no identity connects a factor to declared C2, report an alternative decomposition. |
| 2 | “SIGNFORK has resolved the residual contradiction.” | Hybrid learned/exact background and mixed-horizon Ψ remain even after a price×gate fork. The exact gate may be mathematically inert. | **20–40 min, no physics:** compare the two existing score-construction paths line by line; audit cached base/singleton/joint field and boundary identities, and whether a gate changes only empty/singleton zeros. Reconcile full/additive score identities before interpreting the fork. |
| 3 | “C1REAL found an information ceiling” or “EXACTGEN made the model deployable.” | Finite estimator failure is not non-identifiability; exact features may require candidate solves or differ from runtime inputs. | **30–45 min, no fitting:** inspect feature suppliers and archived train/held-out definitions, target lineage, duplicate groups, scaling and availability. Tabulate each of the 16 inputs' acquisition path and online cost. A proved collision bounds only its supported population. |
| 4 | “+78% survives a causal implementation and combines with corrected provisioning.” | Perfect prior SINR is available on failed/no-mode records; feedback precision, timing and cost are idealized; corrected provisioning changes the opportunity. | **20–40 min, no simulation:** audit R2/R3's timestamp/history code and join existing record categories to its feedback assumptions. State which feedback requires pilots despite no decode. If no observation contract supports it, label the number ideal-feedback, not deployed. A new numerical gain under another law remains UNDETERMINED. |
| 5 | “All demand-capped headlines use the same reported objective.” | Endpoint capping versus per-boundary capping; full-buffer production summaries versus diagnostic caps; best-found versus reference denominator. | **15–30 min, no physics:** compare cap placement and units in the four existing scorers; inspect per-user receipt schema and printed pooled totals. Reconcile the provenance of +0.273%. Do not silently replace one traffic model by another. |
| 6 | “All certified endpoints are already optimized for the reported objective.” | Fixed-price, boundary-0 objective differs from capped 48-boundary pooled EE; two-swap failure is being generalized to singleton failure. | **10–30 min, existing receipts:** read certificate objective/horizon and the two capped swap rows. Before OBJMISMATCH arrives, write which neighbourhood its claim covers. Any zero result needs complete coverage, not just no improvement among sampled moves. |
| 7 | “The large full-minus-drop result proves useful three-route design.” | Neutral-arm collapse, source intervention confused with knockout, or post-treatment filtering. | **20–40 min, arithmetic only:** compare FULL, all-neutral, each drop and an independent strong reference on the full scheduled population. Print their absolute bits, energy and EE; label any restricted subset as conditional. Keep source benefit and architecture benefit separate. |
| 8 | “The exact pipeline costs 29.42 hours and training can start on that projection.” | Both anchor timings used 992 rows but different execution scope; model inputs, coalition work, legal-action coverage and endpoints are excluded. | **20–40 min, no timing run:** reconcile existing work counters, switches, tape sizes, fields and boundaries for 49.03 and 632.83 seconds. Cost the actual proposed protocol as separate setup, source, coalition, training and evaluation terms; flag unmeasured terms. |
| 9 | “Positive counts settle service and substantiality.” | At-least-one-decode service, individual losers, small date count and an unfixed practical bar. | **15–30 min, existing ledger:** retain 39/800 losses and attainment alongside pooled gain; reconcile 6/20 versus 1/20; list unique dates and reused carriers. Specify the practical decision criterion prospectively, not by choosing among observed headline percentages. |

**Prospective reading rules for the five pending measurements.**

These rules interpret results; they do not authorize runs or alter the existing experiment. If a job has already completed, the rules remain prospective to my reading because I have not opened its output. A validity failure should be reported as such, preserving the original result; it is not permission to hunt for a favourable rerun.

**OBJMISMATCH.** A legal single-user move improving capped committed EE disproves the relevant endpoint's local optimality **for that objective and neighbourhood**. It does not invalidate its old fixed-price certificate. Count all tested endpoints, the number with improving moves, and the attainable reported gain, with bits, joules and guard semantics. A high flip rate with negligible gain means mismatch without demonstrated practical importance. A small number of large gains means concentrated opportunity, not universal failure.

A complete negative census establishes local optimality only on the tested legal singleton neighbourhood. A sampled negative result means “none found.” Neither excludes other starts, swaps or coordinated controls. Also distinguish per-anchor ratio optimization from whole-panel ratio optimization. With positive energy, a candidate improves the panel when `ΔN−eta_panel*ΔE>0`, where `eta_panel` is the current pooled ratio. Testing against each anchor's own eta answers a different question. A hindsight gain does not establish causal recoverability, C1 learnability, or that merely changing eta resolves the snapshot-versus-horizon mismatch.

**C1REAL.** First authenticate the exact target, physical lineage, feature values and split. “Same 16 inputs” must mean the same deployable information, not simply 16 slots populated by a more expensive evaluator. A strong held-out predictor on those admissible inputs demonstrates predictability on that support and weakens an architectural explanation tied to the smaller model. Good within-user ordering but poor catalogue top choice indicates that composition or cross-user scale remains a problem; good value prediction alone settles neither.

Failure of all tested estimators leaves the architectural-versus-informational cause **UNDETERMINED** unless there is additional identification evidence. Exact same-input/different-target cases prove ambiguity for those cases; quantify their mass and whether they reverse relevant decisions. Absence of observed collisions does not prove sufficiency. A model that succeeds only after reading coupled candidate outcomes establishes an oracle-feature result. Under no outcome should R², loss or ordering be restated as an EE gain. Under no outcome does target predictability alone prove the benefit of informative-source training.

**EXACTGEN.** A pass means a specified set of rows faithfully implements a specified target and input contract, with authenticated source, fields, boundary grids, references, prices, Phi and three-offset semantics. It does not mean that a flag change alone repaired the deployed inference path. Require baseline/self-action identities and same-path base/singleton/joint construction; verify numerical units and the difference between exact arithmetic over binary64 receipts and exact physical truth. A zero algebraic identity residual cannot authenticate the semantics of its operands.

Report row inclusion and coalition coverage, including empty/singleton handling, grand rows and missing sizes; legality filtering can change the training population. Separate target generation from inference-feature acquisition. For cost reconciliation, equal row counts do not imply equal work. If 49.03 and 632.83 seconds are reconciled by boundary count, optional coalition work or execution settings, state that mechanism and scope the rate accordingly. If not, cost is **UNDETERMINED**, not “affordable because one receipt says so.” Partial completion is an exact partial corpus, not a completed corpus. A complete corpus is readiness evidence, never EE evidence.

**SIGNFORK.** Require all four cells to share physical world, anchor set, action catalogue, candidate outcomes, additive background, residual definition and guard, except the two named factors. Print the two price effects separately at each gate setting and the two gate effects separately at each price setting; do not describe an averaged effect as universal if the interaction is large. Changes must be in committed reported bits/energy, not only argmax or surrogate score.

If changing price helps under both gates, that supports a price effect **in that fixed experiment**. If the gate matters under both prices, inspect which formerly zero/missing rows changed and whether the intervention replaced the residual object. If only their combination helps, the interpretation is an interaction; neither factor alone is the explanation. If neither matters, the contradiction remains unresolved; learned-versus-exact additive background, horizon mixing, catalogue and physical lineage remain candidates. If the exact residual is zero wherever contexts are absent, a null gate effect is expected algebraically and says nothing about the learned head's scale.

Do not call a favourable cell a new operating rule. Do not assert that one world's four cells reconcile the two original reports unless you can transport their score definitions and reproduce each original treatment under the matched construction. Retain +5.62% and the approximately −60% hybrid changed-subset result with their different meanings until that is done.

**FACTORIAL.** Before any sign is read, require eight distinct **factor settings** `000…111`, plus the external nearest-eligible BASELINE as a ninth reference unless an explicit identity establishes coincidence. An exact `000` score may tie-break to a nonbaseline candidate; it is not automatically the trained all-neutral control. Distinguish exact factor removal from neutral-source retraining. Identify how C2 is represented: a genuine three-offset continuation, the sealed oracle tie-break, or an alternative partition of immediate singleton surplus. These are not interchangeable. Under the sealed oracle tie-break, zero C2 effect with a unique primary maximum is expected and is not evidence that learned Q2 cannot help proposals.

For each route report standalone benefit `eta({i})−eta(000)` and conditional benefit `eta(111)−eta(111\{i})`, plus full versus external baseline, each with an explicit relative denominator when expressed as a percentage. A factorial interaction is a difference of those effects on a chosen scale, not the physical Ψ. If prices are re-optimized per cell, the results are whole-procedure effects including re-pricing; if fixed, name the common price. A full exact score must reconstruct the intended objective before it can supply any upper bound.

A large full span with small singles can mean complementarity; a large full span with one dominant single may satisfy the owner's revised goal while providing little reason for the other routes. Large leave-one-out effects with weak full-versus-strong-reference performance indicate dependence within this design, not a strong design. A small full span bounds the fixed catalogue's opportunity only if FULL really is its reported-objective optimum under the same constraints. It does not prove all decompositions, catalogues or causal policies futile. A negative residual marginal in a fixed-price proxy factorial need not be impossible; a full optimum losing to another cell under the identical reporting objective and feasible catalogue demands a semantics/optimization reconciliation.

Finally, a positive exact factorial does **not** pass a learned-source claim or demonstrate learnability. Under the owner's revised goal, report magnitudes without inventing a numerical “substantial” threshold after seeing them. If no prospective practical threshold exists, the mechanical G1 pass/fail is **UNDETERMINED** and the result is a planning input. This is a limit on the conclusion, not a reason to commission another open-ended audit cycle.

The records already contain enough information to prevent the next fake success metric. The missing action is to bind each conclusion to the intervention that actually produced its number, before using it to decide what should be trained.

